{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation","id":382269,"title":"3E Lunars facts and speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T13:57:08-08:00","id":382269,"title":"3E Lunars facts and speculation","content":"Decided to start this thread after some discussions we've been having in another lunar thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms\">So, if Lunars can't use MA in animal forms...</a>). It got me thinking about what we really know about 3E Lunars. While the book may not be out for a while, it's always fun to gather facts and speculate! <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm admitted not the best person to start this as I haven't been following Lunar's that closely, but I'll try and update this first post with any confirmed facts that get gathered together. So what have I seen from the Devs so far:<br /> <br /> <b>- Lunar's are going to be a &quot;viable&quot; (don't shoot me John) option in 3E.</b> For those who played 2E, that's already a huge bonus!<br /> <b>- Lunar's no longer live on the borders of Creation... or at least most of them don't.</b><br /> <b>- The Lunar concept has less to do with the Wyld then in previous editions.</b> This will be interesting as it raises a lot of questions.<br /> <b>- Lunar abilities and charms are being balanced against their shapeshifting, so you can play a Lunar that doesn't do a lot of shapeshifting and still have a lot to offer.</b> This is a big one as in 2E, you were either a shapeshifter or you were useless (maybe a bit harsh)<br /> <b>- Animals are being designed from the ground up with Lunar shapeshifting in mind.</b> Another huge plus, because in 2E animals seemed really &quot;tacked on&quot; and not all that interesting. One type of bird was hardly different to another. The addition of unique abilities for each animal will really add to a shapechanging Lunar's toolbox. Hopefully the system/variety of animals continues to grow giving Lunar's a lot to play with.<br /> <br /> Well that's all I can think of off the top of my head. I'll do a little digging and see if I can't add to the &quot;what we know&quot; section. Let me know if anyone has seen other messages from the Devs, and I'll add those as well.<br /> <br /> I'm really excited about Lunar's, which honestly is surprising. I came into Exalted in early 2E, so Lunar's have always sounded interesting but had crap mechanics. I'm especially interested in some of their new back story. If they've lost a lot of that &quot;Wyld tainted&quot; background, it generates a dozen questions. Why are there only 3 castes instead of 5 now? What causes chimerism, or is that still a thing (hope it is because they make interesting enemies)? What happened to them after the Usurpation if they didn't flee into the Wyld like in previous editions? Is Raksi still bat-shit crazy, and what is suppose to be the cause if not the Wyld taint? Needless to say, I'm almost as excited by the Lunar's as I am by a revamp of my Abyssals! <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:04:29-08:00","id":382295,"title":"","content":"Has it been confirmed that they are going to keep the 'there are 3 castes now but there used to be 5' thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:10:04-08:00","id":382300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382295#post382295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been confirmed that they are going to keep the 'there are 3 castes now but there used to be 5' thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge. This is one of those things where we have to speculate based solely on 1E/2E material. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-26-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:10:32-08:00","id":382302,"title":"","content":"Other Lunar stuff:<br /> <br /> <b>-Lunars in animal forms may not be able to use supernatural Martial Arts if the form doesn't make sense for it. </b>A Lunar in python form can't use Snake Style, lacking the limbs needed to emulate a snake, while being a snake. lulz. In gorilla form, maybe they can still use Snake Style, being humanoid in shape?<br /> <b>-Lunars in DBT form will lose some or all of their access to the Evocations they've unlocked on their Artifacts</b>. This has to do with how much of your power you're &quot;wearing on the outside.&quot; Possible comparisons to Sidereals being the &quot;worst&quot; at Evocations but also the splat with easiest access to SMA, which is another &quot;externally-worn&quot; power. Very well may lead to a lot more in-combat shifting in and out of DBT to gain DBT-specific benefits and Evocation-specific benefits as the tactical situation merits. Which would be fucking cool!<br /> <b>-Lunars are no longer solely dependent on DBT as the keystone of an optimal combat build.</b> Statements were made that most Lunars will probably learn DBT when newly-Exalted since it's a quick, cheap boost to their power, but a good percentage will largely abandon it as a main tactic once they start unlocking Evocations or other, deeper builds which are competitive with DBT but more expensive to build to. Probably also because it's easier to pass off as a god or other kind of Exalt when you're not in Crinos, without sacrificing potency for doing so.<br /> <b>-Lunars can learn the &quot;techniques&quot; of animals they turn into, which allow them to fight even better as that animal.</b> Ex. the Tyrant Lizard's terrifying signature bite attack.<br /> <b>-Lunar themes are going to be more tied to Gaia, as animals are of Gaia. </b>Whatever this means!<br /> <b>-Knacks as a concept, if they return, will not be there solely to differentiate vs Charms to prevent Eclipse Charmshare from learning them. </b>If they come back, it might be for reasons of mixed-Attribute-prereq effect trees, probably in shapeshifting (i.e. tier 1 is Perception based, tier 2 is Stamina, Tier 3 is Wits, etc). It's an organization that would be really screwy in &quot;true&quot; native Charms and remind people of 1e Charmcloud but might make sense for shapeshifting powers.<br /> <b>-I think it was confirmed that formlock is dead. </b>Or at least enough authors hate it such that it probably won't be as terrible and crippling as it was before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-26-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:14:55-08:00","id":382310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382295#post382295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been confirmed that they are going to keep the 'there are 3 castes now but there used to be 5' thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are, but the story behind how that came to be is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:22:45-08:00","id":382316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382310#post382310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are, but the story behind how that came to be is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh, tidbit of information to get us speculating... I see what you did there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:26:04-08:00","id":382320,"title":"","content":"<b>-Chimerism is now an accepted state, and simply refers to Lunars customizing their spirit shape</b><b>.</b> It is no longer a horrible malignancy that melts a Lunar into a big boring blob of crazy. It is mentioned this was to enable hybrid beast shapes for those who find a single animal too limiting. It has basically nothing in common with what it used to be.<br /> <b>-Lunars still have spirit shape, which may now play bigger roles than in past editions.</b> The specifics aren't known, and haven't been mentioned in ages, but John once mused about a system of associated keywords that would allow a Lunar to rearrange where some Charms fall in the set and make them accessible at favored costs.<br /> Expanding on the bullet point about Lunars no longer being tied down in the Wyld:<br /> <b>-More Lunars now have</b> <b>dominions within Creation, the largest of which is a big island known as the Caul.</b> The Caul is warred over with the Realm -- it's an important trading spot -- and events have led to it being taken &quot;off the grid&quot; of the Loom of Fate. Lunars have managed to install a sort of Fate-analogue in its place. It is suggested this doesn't operate quite so well as the Loom, but specifics remain to be seen.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> be some recommended reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-26-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:53:11-08:00","id":382402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382302#post382302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Lunar stuff:<br /> <b>-Lunar themes are going to be more tied to Gaia, as animals are of Gaia. </b>Whatever this means!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. The connection between Lunars and animals is from the connection between Luna and Gaia. This infers that animals are not a default state of Lunars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:08:51-08:00","id":382410,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I had something for the Lunar Gaia thing, but can't remember... wait, now I do. I've been watching a lot of David Attenborough documentaries lately, and among the things they make me think about Lunars is &quot;if Luna represents adaptability and Gaia represents life, then Luna might be drawn to Gaia and favour animal forms and have some of those associations descend to her Chosen because life is the most adaptable thing in existence&quot;. Like, there are frogs that live in the rainforest that don't give a fuck about the lack of standing water being kind of impractical for amphibians; they just raise tadpoles in the water that accumulates in bell shaped plants, feeding them on their own unfertilised eggs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:11:21-08:00","id":382411,"title":"","content":"Half of me is thrilled that they're revisiting things to &quot;bake it in&quot; better. Animals (and resulting mutations) for one. The Spirit Shape as well (which has always been a pet peeve of mine). I'm <u><b>exceedingly</b></u> happy to see that Chimera are no longer a problem (in the sense that I can &quot;be me&quot; as opposed to a humanoid representative of my furry friends in the animal kingdom). The death of form-lock is also tantalizing (maybe I won't have to default to DBT and murder everyone in order to conceal my human identity).<br /> <br /> The other half of me worries with the Gaia stuff (but this might be old WtA fears) of a furry-fest (in having played games where Lunar &quot;culture&quot;, tattoos, chimerism, etc were all used like clubs to smack us over the head if we had no interest in their tribal furry-frolicking in the forest).<br /> <br /> Which half wins depends on whether it leans &quot;Smokey the Bear on steroids&quot; vs &quot;god-beast who reshapes the environment in passing&quot;. <br /> <br /> All the while (and not to derail) this makes me wonder how Infernals will do (as I loved their mutations and Shintai implementation more than the entire Lunar splat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:22:02-08:00","id":382419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382310#post382310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are, but the story behind how that came to be is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I feel justified in assuming it will be better. Previous work quality aside, I can't see how it would be possible to do worse then 'we spent too much time out there in the Wyld ****ing animals and it melted our exaltations a bit'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:52:12-08:00","id":382463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382320#post382320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-Chimerism is now an accepted state, and simply refers to Lunars customizing their spirit shape</b><b>.</b> It is no longer a horrible malignancy that melts a Lunar into a big boring blob of crazy. It is mentioned this was to enable hybrid beast shapes for those who find a single animal too limiting. It has basically nothing in common with what it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will there still be Lunars who have lost themselves in their uncontrolled transformations? That is just a really cool possibility for storytelling, maybe it could be like gremlinized Alchemicals, where you have to willingly start down a corrupting path of charms for it to happen, that way it isn't something that could happen to any character, you have to make a conscious choice to temp fate in the search for greater power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:55:53-08:00","id":382465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382463#post382463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there still be Lunars who have lost themselves in their uncontrolled transformations? That is just a really cool possibility for storytelling, maybe it could be like gremlinized Alchemicals, where you have to willingly start down a corrupting path of charms for it to happen, that way it isn't something that could happen to any character, you have to make a conscious choice to temp fate in the search for greater power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does it need a mechanical basis at all? Could be purely narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:14:23-08:00","id":382494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382465#post382465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it need a mechanical basis at all? Could be purely narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could, but I personally like to have at least some mechanical framework to these things. I think the Alchemicals did it very well, except it was just a little bit too easy to slip down that slope, once you chose to start on it that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 01-26-2015, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:35:18-08:00","id":382503,"title":"","content":"<b>-Illusions are no longer a Lunar thing, nor do they have any sort of Druid-like powers for commanding/controlling reality.</b> Their power is rooted more in command of the self and in shaping perceptions of themselves. The latter lends itself to taking on some effects that used to be illusions for Lunars, and the former doesn't necessarily preclude changes-to-oneself that can impact things beyond oneself (<a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0121.html\" target=\"_blank\">pheromones</a> were a given example*).<br /> <br /> * Not necessarily for use in neutralizing knock-out gas, but y'never know!<br /> <br /> <b>-Lunars will be able to learn multiple options for shapestealing.</b>When last mentioned, hunting someone for heart's blade is still the default, but the devs want to give a lot of options. One of the old means, sleeping with someone, was explicitly noted; intimacy-related shape-taking (of some sort) is already in the plans; and hatewheel agreed with someone who noted that &quot;physicality is a part of form taking, not so much observation.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>-&quot;[The Solar/Lunar Bond is] a whole big complicated thing with huge bearing on what the Lunars are doing, rather than a very simple brain lasso.&quot;</b> Direct quote from Holden (okay, okay, not counting the brackets &gt;.&gt; ). The Bond is looking to be very different than it was. They've mentioned not planning to make it a mechanics-heavy thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:04:18-08:00","id":382602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382463#post382463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will there still be Lunars who have lost themselves in their uncontrolled transformations? That is just a really cool possibility for storytelling, maybe it could be like gremlinized Alchemicals, where you have to willingly start down a corrupting path of charms for it to happen, that way it isn't something that could happen to any character, you have to make a conscious choice to temp fate in the search for greater power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be a component of the Lunar story for EX3. There's no Wyld taint or any other tie to another power that might make it possible. Any &quot;dark side&quot; narratives would probably center on how far they're willing to go in terms of external actions to take down the Realm and the consequences of those actions, not how neatly they walk on a razor's edge of corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:41:16-08:00","id":382623,"title":"","content":"The other problem with the &quot;Wyld taint&quot; is that it is <u>firm proof</u> that Lunar Exaltations could be diminished/altered/lessened. Kind of flies in the face of Exaltation being eternal and invincible and stuff --- and opens avenues to &quot;well, if exposure to the Wyld could do that, maybe I can expose them to other things to ruin them more&quot;.<br /> <br /> I welcome Chimera as a deliberate and viable choice.<br /> <br /> You can still be a Chimera by choice <u>and</u> a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:46:02-08:00","id":382624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382623#post382623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other problem with the &quot;Wyld taint&quot; is that it is <u>firm proof</u> that Lunar Exaltations could be diminished/altered/lessened. Kind of flies in the face of Exaltation being eternal and invincible and stuff --- and opens avenues to &quot;well, if exposure to the Wyld could do that, maybe I can expose them to other things to ruin them more&quot;.<br /> <br /> I welcome Chimera as a deliberate and viable choice.<br /> <br /> You can still be a Chimera by choice <u>and</u> a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of the major splats are already examples of 'altered' exaltations, so wyld corruption is hardly the only thing contradicting the fact that exaltations are supposedly indestructible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:46:30-08:00","id":382625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382602#post382602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't seem to be a component of the Lunar story for EX3. There's no Wyld taint or any other tie to another power that might make it possible. Any &quot;dark side&quot; narratives would probably center on how far they're willing to go in terms of external actions to take down the Realm and the consequences of those actions, not how neatly they walk on a razor's edge of corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just kinda bums me out, that potential to become the actual monster was one of the things I thought was a good part of Lunars. I didn't like that that you had to reign in your character's actions to avoid having it happening, but I would love to see that potential to become an actual monster not just a monstrous person be re-introduced in some other way. It didn't work as a sort of contemporary to Limit, but I do hope there is still room for it.<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see how Ma-Ha-Suchi is done in EX3, without some sort of chimerism he ends up in a weird place, is he just sitting there on his throne saying &quot;Look at what thy did to me!&quot; for the hell of it? His major grievance is pretty dependent on at least some potential for Lunars to come undone and loose themselves. Maybe he will just be mentally ill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:53:44-08:00","id":382629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll be interested to see how Ma-Ha-Suchi is done in EX3, without some sort of chimerism he ends up in a weird place, is he just sitting there on his throne saying &quot;Look at what thy did to me!&quot; for the hell of it? His major grievance is pretty dependent on at least some potential for Lunars to come undone and loose themselves. Maybe he will just be mentally ill? </div> </div> </div><br /> Just because the wyld isn't going to have warped the exaltation anymore doesn't mean individual lunars can't still have been warped by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:56:30-08:00","id":382632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382625#post382625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This just kinda bums me out, that potential to become the actual monster was one of the things I thought was a good part of Lunars. I didn't like that that you had to reign in your character's actions to avoid having it happening, but I would love to see that potential to become an actual monster not just a monstrous person be re-introduced in some other way. It didn't work as a sort of contemporary to Limit, but I do hope there is still room for it.<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see how Ma-Ha-Suchi is done in EX3, without some sort of chimerism he ends up in a weird place, is he just sitting there on his throne saying &quot;Look at what thy did to me!&quot; for the hell of it? His major grievance is pretty dependent on at least some potential for Lunars to come undone and loose themselves. Maybe he will just be mentally ill?</div> </div> </div> </div>He'd probably go back to what he was in 1e, i.e. not a venal excuse to make references to Meatloaf songs, but a mighty warlord poised to threaten the River Province with conquest. Lunars aren't the type of character to go fully off the edge like that. I'm not sure that any Exalted really fulfill that kind of niche, nor can we be sure if Alchemicals will retain the potential for Apostasy. That sort of story is really more the forte of <i>Double Cross</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:08:30-08:00","id":382653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382629#post382629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just because the wyld isn't going to have warped the exaltation anymore doesn't mean individual lunars can't still have been warped by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, maybe he ran into something in the Wyld beyond even an elder exalt's ability to shrug of? That would be cool, maybe you could do away with the twisted chimera as a core mechanic of all Lunars, but introduce some of the beasties as like canon monsters with write ups. Lunars who went too deep into the Wyld and came back permanently twisted into shifting beasts, take them out of the player space, but give them some mechanical thought so a DM can introduce them or even have a PC start down that path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:43:32-08:00","id":382665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altered is not the same as diminished, one of those alterations is traditionally considered to be reversible(Even if it's not going to be mandatory for &quot;good guys&quot; anymore) and the other was done by multiple World Creating Eldritch Abominations.<br /> <br /> I think those get a pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that DotFA showed us the two lost castes, they were less then impressive. So it is kind of arguable whether it was even a lessening or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T21:04:18-08:00","id":382698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382625#post382625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be interested to see how Ma-Ha-Suchi is done in EX3, without some sort of chimerism he ends up in a weird place, is he just sitting there on his throne saying &quot;Look at what thy did to me!&quot; for the hell of it? His major grievance is pretty dependent on at least some potential for Lunars to come undone and loose themselves. Maybe he will just be mentally ill?</div> </div> </div> </div>There really isn't anything about Ma-Ha-Suchi that depends on Lunars having some devolving into horrible monstrosities mechanic.<br /> <br /> He <i>definitely</i> won't suddenly be portrayed as mentally ill. Equating mental illness with evil is a hella prominent thing that is hella gross, and not something I'd really want to contribute to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 01-27-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T01:46:37-08:00","id":382823,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I'm really frustrated by the whole David Attenborough thing, because all of this stuff I'm learning about fauna across the world is absolutely fascinating in the same way that learning about historical and anthropological and economic things is...<br /> <br /> But unlike those things, I can't apply any of it to Exalted! Exalted can be a lot of things, but it's not really capable of incorporating the activities of wildlife in any particularly important manner. I doubt there are really any roleplaying games that can, except Chuubo's*.<br /> <br /> Yet, I can't help but feel that some of it could be salvaged for Lunars. Not so much with using their shapeshifting to put them into stories of wildlife survival as applying some of the broad concepts evident in the variety and survival strategies of living things as a guiding image of what the Lunar milieu is.<br /> <br /> At the very least, I'm attaching to the image that the Lunar presence in the wilderness (to which the politics of the Age of Sorrows has forced them to flee and which they can make themselves at home in by their own nature) resembles some of the activities of animals, as opposed to Solars who seem more likely to follow the form and function of hermits, or even characters like Tarzan. In this way, I can reconcile the idea that Lunars have an advantage, or at least a resonance, with these scenarios that doesn't rub against the fact that Survival is still an Ability Solars can have, with all that that implies.<br /> <br /> * You can portray basically any story with Chuubo's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T02:22:52-08:00","id":382828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382624#post382624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the major splats are already examples of 'altered' exaltations, so wyld corruption is hardly the only thing contradicting the fact that exaltations are supposedly indestructible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars aren't at risk of spontaneously mutating into Abyssals-or-Infernals as a result of botching a roll on a <i>routine use of their exaltation's defining trait</i> when they wander too close to the Underworld-or-Mafeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T03:44:23-08:00","id":382868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382410#post382410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit, I had something for the Lunar Gaia thing, but can't remember... wait, now I do. I've been watching a lot of David Attenborough documentaries lately, and among the things they make me think about Lunars is &quot;if Luna represents adaptability and Gaia represents life, then Luna might be drawn to Gaia and favour animal forms and have some of those associations descend to her Chosen because life is the most adaptable thing in existence&quot;. Like, there are frogs that live in the rainforest that don't give a fuck about the lack of standing water being kind of impractical for amphibians; they just raise tadpoles in the water that accumulates in bell shaped plants, feeding them on their own unfertilised eggs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, egg-feeding obligates are the coolest! The way in which males and females take on different roles in the transportation, protection, and rearing of their offspring is absolutely fascinating.<br /> <br /> (Note: I keep/breed dart frogs, though I don't have any obligate egg feeders at the moment, since they're tougher to take care of properly. If I cannot make a Dart-Frog Lunar with awesome climby/sneaky/poison powers, appearance based magic for bright colors and seductive music, and some kickass medium-range tongue-based combat in 3E, I will be a sad Guru.<br /> <br /> Seriously, dart frogs are like if songbirds were tiny and poisonous and adorkable.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:40:37-08:00","id":382930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382625#post382625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His major grievance is pretty dependent on at least some potential for Lunars to come undone and loose themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the major grievance of Ma-Ha-Suchi should be revised a bit from bitterness over not being pretty anymore?<br /> <br /> I'm all for highly personalized and kind of petty motivations for epic heroes, but I think that one goes a bit too far.<br /> <br /> It could still be a bit of a sticking point for him, a bit of a Ratigan-esque trigger that gets you eaten by goatfolk if you bring it up in his presence, but not as far as &quot;I can't look in the fucking mirror, damn, I will kill everyone in the world!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T06:52:03-08:00","id":383036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382302#post382302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-Lunar themes are going to be more tied to Gaia, as animals are of Gaia. </b>Whatever this means!</div> </div> </div> </div>This will probably be something I toss on it's ass, mostly because I'm of the opinion that, if we <i>need</i> to have Exalts that have Gaiaian themes/mechanics/whatevers, it definitely shouldn't be Lunars. I think it's much more fitting for Dragon-Blodded, what with the minor thing of being the Exalted of the Five Elemental Dragons and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382828#post382828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars aren't at risk of spontaneously mutating into Abyssals-or-Infernals as a result of botching a roll on a <i>routine use of their exaltation's defining trait</i> when they wander too close to the Underworld-or-Mafeas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something something something Paradox.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:38:24-08:00","id":383087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382930#post382930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps the major grievance of Ma-Ha-Suchi should be revised a bit from bitterness over not being pretty anymore?<br /> <br /> I'm all for highly personalized and kind of petty motivations for epic heroes, but I think that one goes a bit too far.<br /> <br /> It could still be a bit of a sticking point for him, a bit of a Ratigan-esque trigger that gets you eaten by goatfolk if you bring it up in his presence, but not as far as &quot;I can't look in the fucking mirror, damn, I will kill everyone in the world!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>His trigger shouldn't be his appearance, because he probably did that millennia ago. If the character still needs one, his trigger should make him kind of like the Lunar equivalent of Peleps Deled - if you don't hate the Realm enough, you're the one who gets to be an example to everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:41:59-08:00","id":383093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383087#post383087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His trigger shouldn't be his appearance, because he probably did that millennia ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow the logic here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:52:09-08:00","id":383106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383093#post383093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow the logic here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I''ll offer my interpretation:<br /> <br /> With the Lunars no longer being nerfed in regards to the Wyld, there's no fucking way that a shapeshifting host of Exalted would be incapable of trivially reversing any physical mutation inflicted on them. Likewise, Wyld Taint and Chimerism are not things the Wyld could inflict on their Exaltations.<br /> <br /> Mutations, Chimerism, and Lost Castes are things the Lunars DID TO THEMSELVES.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi deliberately changed from a Goat Totem to a wolf-goat Baphomet Totem. If he's not as pretty as he used to be, he deliberately made himself uglier.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi is not history's whipping boy. He's not a whining child. He's mad as Hell about the Golden First Age that the Dragon-Blooded destroyed, mad at the Solar Exalted for being foolish enough to fall for it, mad at himself and the other Lunar Exalted for letting it happen...<br /> <br /> But his brokenness and debased current self are deliberate choices made in hateful, defiant response to those failures. He transformed himself into a weapon of death against the Shogunate, and then the Pretender Realm.<br /> <br /> We can probably expect to see more of the Ma-Ha-Suchi we saw in the comic where he backfists Bear Fist for losing to Panther in a fight, and then excuses his behavior with Dace by muttering &quot;I owed him a debt from another life&quot;, and then screams that he won't fail Creation again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:05:33-08:00","id":383119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383106#post383106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi deliberately changed from a Goat Totem to a wolf-goat Baphomet Totem. If he's not as pretty as he used to be, he deliberately made himself uglier.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi is not history's whipping boy. He's not a whining child. He's mad as Hell about the Golden First Age that the Dragon-Blooded destroyed, mad at the Solar Exalted for being foolish enough to fall for it, mad at himself and the other Lunar Exalted for letting it happen...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that precludes the possibility that he doesn't necessarily like what he looks like, even if he's deliberately adopted it as a matter of statement and pragmatism, and staring at him for too long might make him a little bit twitchy.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could just be that Ma-Ha-Suchi has always been unattractive and kind of touchy about it, and long bitter experience combined with the Great Curse exacerbates that (and he has personal or practical reasons to not just permanently disguise himself).<br /> <br /> I don't want it to be a big, central thing for him, the defining feature that his motivations and personality revolve around, but I'm still a bit attached to him having some references to the Beast from the French story, including occasions where he rages about people who have come to stare at him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:20:30-08:00","id":383130,"title":"","content":"As grotesque as this might be, I've always interpreted Ma Ha Suchi as a satyr like being, with all the hedonism it entails, corrupted into a Baphomet &quot;satanic&quot; symbol of the beast kind of figure. He's certainly mad over the events of the Usurpation, and has consolidated his power, raided nearby settlements and made an army of Beastmen, both powerful and perverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:32:05-08:00","id":383155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be drastically misinterpreting this, but I've heard that in 1E, the fist step towards Chimerism was Sprit Shape changing from one animal to another while keeping a few traits from the original animal.<br /> <br /> Goat to wolf with a goat's horns and hooves, for example.<br /> <br /> If MahawahI'msougly is a Chimera by 3E's deifintion, he probably did his &quot;Wolf with goat horns&quot; thing to himself.<br /> <br /> Of Course, if he screwed up his Chimerism and gave himself the &quot;horns and hooves in all forms thing&quot; and he became a Chimera around the time of the usurpation, he could well pull a Doctor Doom and blame it on the Sids/Solars/Dragon Blooded/X when it's really his fault in the first place-especially if his Human Form isn't actually all that Ugly beyond the horns and he's just so vain that he can't see beyond his one flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimerism in 1e was actually like chimerism in 2e, only with fewer rules about how it happened. Switching your totem was seen as courting chimerahood, but obviously if you had tattoos, nothing was going to come of it. 2e just made the state of affairs worse by making it a mechanically-preferred state to be in, which could technically be had by cutting off only half of your Limit bar, collecting your cool new powers, and going on your merry way.The taboo against totem mixing was ported over to 2e as well, kind of, in the form of Perfected Hybrid Interaction, with the same nonsensical line about other Lunars looking down on it as &quot;courting chimerism&quot;. EX3 is a change in that it's reassigning the term &quot;Chimera&quot; to mean the formerly somewhat taboo practice of mixing totems from 1e, and making it acceptable, with no Wyld-tainted knockoffs of The Thing to be seen, at least not among the Lunars. <br /> <br /> As for Ma-Ha-Suchi, his 1e description, upon re-reading, does in fact seem to make him like the Lunar Deled. He requires zealous hatred of the Realm from his beastmen brood, and while a courteous host to all who offer him proper respect, will sacrifice even other Lunars to Luna at one of the many celebrations of the Bloody Huntress that he regularly and frequently holds. His goat-wolf-man-ness is never mentioned as being important or an underlying cause of any of his personal &quot;quirks&quot; regarding the hatred of the Realm. He's simply a god-chief plotting war, and he has designs on using the Scavenger Lands as the head of his spear against the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-27-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:53:52-08:00","id":383165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382698#post382698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really isn't anything about Ma-Ha-Suchi that depends on Lunars having some devolving into horrible monstrosities mechanic.<br /> <br /> He <i>definitely</i> won't suddenly be portrayed as mentally ill. Equating mental illness with evil is a hella prominent thing that is hella gross, and not something I'd really want to contribute to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying a characters delusions could be fuel for their evil acts is not the same as saying all mental illness = evil. If Ma-Ha-Suchi has delusions of persecution which drive him on a vindictive campaign against all those who he imagines to have &quot;wronged&quot; him, I would say he is mentally ill. Mental illness whether it be psychopathy or paranoid delusions can cause people to commit evil acts, and honestly I think it should be part of the narrative conversation with most villains. Do they have a legitimate motivation for their acts, or are they operating on a general disregard for the well being of others, and a delusional view of the world?<br /> <br /> Somebody who starts a bar-room brawl may just have some simple psychological anger management issues, somebody who leads an army of goat-men against the world over imaginary sleights from a millennium ago, while completely ignoring their own despicable actions...that is a mental illness!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:13:16-08:00","id":383213,"title":"","content":"Don't really know what Ma-Ha-Tsuchi's deal is going to be now. Who knows, maybe his Solar mate thought they'd prank him for being vain. Asked him to transform into a goat-wolf and zapped him with some artifact that forces him to keep horns and hooves in every form he takes! Probably unrealistic, but not completely out of the realm of possibility. Maybe he's pissed about something new that has nothing to do with his previous write-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:13:42-08:00","id":383214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=382823#post382823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* You can portray basically any story with Chuubo's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still struggling to figure out how to get it to do sports anime and tournament arcs. Maybe if I watched more I'd have a better idea.<br /> <br /> (Specifically it's hard to do things where &quot;winning&quot; a competition is important enough that you'd expect the mechanics to tell you whether you win or lose. I don't have a good model for determining who would win a bread-baking competition aside from &quot;wing it&quot; or &quot;compare Intentions&quot;, which seems unsatisfying in a story that's specificially about that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:14:59-08:00","id":383216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383214#post383214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still struggling to figure out how to get it to do sports anime. Maybe if I watched more I'd have a better idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sports anime seem like they'd run best on Epic Fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:15:19-08:00","id":383217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383036#post383036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will probably be something I toss on it's ass, mostly because I'm of the opinion that, if we <i>need</i> to have Exalts that have Gaiaian themes/mechanics/whatevers, it definitely shouldn't be Lunars. I think it's much more fitting for Dragon-Blodded, what with the minor thing of being the Exalted of the Five Elemental Dragons and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean you want to get rid of the Lunar Dominion thing? It seems that claim land within Creation to now be a part of your Dominion is at least a soft connection to Gaia!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:30:45-08:00","id":383229,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with Second Edition Lunars is that they kidnapped and force-fed you into drinking the kool-aid.<br /> <br /> In First Edition, Chimera were simply socially frowned upon --- but viable for those who grow (for example, someone who looks like Ma-Ha-Suchi might have started with goat (calm yet head-strong?) or wolf (pack loyalty, feral) -- and after a century or four (of either meditation or warfare) -- transitions to the other beast (goat - the serenity of age? a stronger will? --- wolf - bravery forged in battle? loyalty from new friends?). Chimerism could serve as a symbol of character growth.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, it was illness and madness and often a death sentence by your peers -- a luxury only First Age elders could enjoy (and even then, taken as a sign of their corruption).<br /> <br /> In First Edition, they played up the Barbarian savage part a lot --- but akin to Solars, Terrestrial Lost Eggs, etc, it wasn't absurd to imagine a Lunar who shunned his peers, stuck to the cities, did their own thing.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Wyld Hunt excels at hunting Lunars -- and if they don't scare you off, you have Lunar Elders who will borderline kidnap you to &quot;save&quot; you. The young Lunar can expect -- after Exalting in a moment of epicness -- to soon after be chased or dragged away from home and family (and maybe by the time you return, if you can find the way, they'll all be victims of whatever you were fighting).<br /> <br /> Don't want tattoos? Tough -- either get branded like cattle OR turn into a monster (and the book even mentions that some Lunars won't even <u><i>risk</i></u> you turning into Chimera, forceable tattooing or simply killing the young Lunar and hoping a barbarian gets Exalted in your place).<br /> <br /> Grudgingly accept the tattoos? Fine -- but first you need to go through the Wyld, doing some arcane tests for some artifact-disfigurement we don't want, by people we can't stand. This adds further problems if you want to play characters with religious or ethical quandaries or who simply do better in urban environments. This isn't merely Abyssal-style &quot;you can join a Deathcult&quot; - no, you <u>have</u> to deal with these neo-shamanistic psychotic-Elders.<br /> <br /> .....who then consider that <i>you owe them a debt. </i><br /> <br /> It's 100% feasible and canon-friendly for you to be <i>kidnapped</i> (and thus unable to defend your people), tossed into the Wyld, indoctrinated by ancient god-monsters who will murder or cripple you if you refuse their gifts (or forceably tattoo you) and THEN be held in DEBT to them.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> And before anyone claims this a criticism ala &quot;its bad a splat has a culture&quot; or &quot;its bad a splat has a distinct look&quot; --- um false equivalencies.<br /> <br /> Terrestrials have one massive culture -- with 13 or so sub-variants -- and Outcastes all throughout other regions. They can look completely human to elemental-in-the-flesh.<br /> <br /> Abyssals have multiple Deathlords -- each with distinct regions, social norms, goals -- and ronin are options. They can look completely human, immaculate beauty or decaying undead.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have two major factions -- a few minor ones -- and multiple different Bureaus and specialties to define themselves. They can look completely human and have heaven's artifacts at their disposal to look more unique,<br /> <br /> Lunars get &quot;here's the Silver Pact -- leave your home, adopt our ink, acquire a debt, agree to our mores, become a Wyld shaman and on rare occasions, build a society maybe, if we don't find it too offensive&quot;. Want to hide your tattoos? You're penalized a charm slot. The whole Silver Pact write-up is probably the most extensive antagonist chapter the splat has (even though many seem to drink the kool-aid).<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> (of course, this is all ranting about 2E and I've love to see what happens in 3E, for better or worse)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","user":"RedRiotousRam","date":". 01-27-2015, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:48:08-08:00","id":383242,"title":"","content":"Actually I wonder what tattoos will do now that the Wyld taint isn't the issue. Are tattoos still a thing for Lunars? Personally I always thought the tattoos were pretty cool and distinct. Especially some of the artifact tattoos that existed. I'd like to see the tattoos expanded on in different ways. The artifact tattoos are a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:48:38-08:00","id":383244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383229#post383229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And before anyone claims this a criticism ala &quot;its bad a splat has a culture&quot; or &quot;its bad a splat has a distinct look&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd stick to saying that it's so hyperbolic and extreme that it kind of hurts even any valid points it might make.<br /> <br /> I mean... one is free to interpret the stuff in those terms as much as they're free to interpret anything in any way, but it seems so far afield from what they're actually trying to go for that it mostly amounts to shadow boxing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:59:55-08:00","id":383255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383165#post383165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">somebody who leads an army of goat-men against the world over imaginary sleights from a millennium ago, while completely ignoring their own despicable actions...that is a mental illness!</div> </div> </div> </div>You might have vaguely had a point in the other stuff, insofar as the possibility of references to figures like Ivan the Terrible or Josef Stalin who were probably genuinely mentally ill, but I think your last point is begging the question.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:03:44-08:00","id":383257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383242#post383242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I wonder what tattoos will do now that the Wyld taint isn't the issue. Are tattoos still a thing for Lunars? Personally I always thought the tattoos were pretty cool and distinct. Especially some of the artifact tattoos that existed. I'd like to see the tattoos expanded on in different ways. The artifact tattoos are a good start.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're definitely cool.<br /> <br /> But the mandatory part was just bad -- things cease to be unique or interesting when everyone is <i>obligated </i>to take them on pain of deformity or death.<br /> <br /> I also disliked the &quot;Claw Speak&quot; and resulting tattoo aesthetic. I <u>loved</u> the imagery of tattoos telling your story (such that faced with the Wyld, the tattoos &quot;stabilize you&quot; and declare your &quot;role&quot; to the story-based Wyld storms)...... I just hated everyone looking like tasteless frat boys with gaudy tribal tattoos. I'd much rather a No Moon who resembles Constantine on his cover with actual legible &amp; articulate writing.<br /> <img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20070218192442/uncyclopedia/images/9/90/Constantine_Tattoo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:05:49-08:00","id":383259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383255#post383255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have vaguely had a point in the other stuff, insofar as the possibility of references to figures like Ivan the Terrible or Josef Stalin who were probably genuinely mentally ill, but I think your last point is begging the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Straw man?<br /> <br /> Point is that a Chimera could be a valid and non-monstrous concept. Such transitions in character development can be cool.<br /> <br /> Criticize Ma-Ha-Suchi if you like, I have no dog in that fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:31:01-08:00","id":383278,"title":"","content":"I definitely think it's preferable to make moonsilver tattoos a neat visual signifier of Lunar culture with some possible beneficial effects that players <i>may</i> choose to have done but not something that <i>must</i> be done to avoid turning into John Carpenter's the Thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:37:29-08:00","id":383326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383244#post383244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd stick to saying that it's so hyperbolic and extreme that it kind of hurts even any valid points it might make.</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point remains valid, regardless of fluff (although I'll note your views on my presentation).<br /> <br /> That said, it's &quot;extreme&quot; in the same way as a Dragon-Blooded rejecting the Realm or being an Outcaste; or an Abyssal ronin (of which I saw plenty in Solar groups). To someone who wants to simply play independent, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">the Silver Pact is the extreme change</span> (because on pain of mutation, turning into an NPC and then death, you're rail-roaded into an entire (and probably alien, if you're not a Barbarian) culture.<br /> <br /> Try it with other splats (yes there are similarities - none as serious).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Outcaste Terrestrial ?</b> </span><br /> Awesome! But as soon as you Exalt, you'll have a specialized murder-squad out to kill you -- and simultaneously, a group of Elder Dynastic Terrestrials who are being paid with artifacts &amp; other backgrounds in order to retrieve you.<br /> <br /> You'll then spend a few months on the Blessed Isle (don't worry if you've never lived there before) where you will be educated in a Realm school, adopted by a House and have their jade sigil emblazoned on your skin. If you refuse, your saviors might kill you (it's not hyperbole, it's in the bloody text) -- and if not, every time your anima banner flares, YOU will be burned/frozen/drowned/poisoned/crushed by your Anima Banner.<br /> <br /> After all this, you can then return home to live your life as an Outcaste Terrestrial in an all-Outcaste game on the far reaches of the North.<br /> <br /> AND THIS IS A GENEROUS COMPARISON!<br /> <br /> Another point --- Terrestrials have an entire Dynasty and Realm full of patricians to support their culture. Abyssals have loose things in agreement -- but each Deathlord can have entire undead cities of dead cultures to keep the mood (think of Sijan). Sidereals have all of Yu Shan. Infernals have countless demons to sustain any nascent culture that a mere 50 Exaltations can't actually form.<br /> <br /> Lunars? You get 300 members --- at most. This is a culture? This establishes norms? Are the Beastmen doing wyld tattoos and reading claw speak and all engaging in shamanism, so when the Silver Pact convenes, each Lunar takes with them a few hundred mortals? I mean, a culture should be larger than 10 high school classes worth of demi-gods who might not even speak the same language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383244#post383244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... one is free to interpret the stuff in those terms as much as they're free to interpret anything in any way, but it seems so far afield from what they're actually trying to go for that it mostly amounts to shadow boxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As aforementioned, it's a rant against 2nd Edition not a criticism of 3E -- I'm eagerly awaiting any updates (on Lunars and Infernals).<br /> <br /> My main criticism is &quot;why make something <b><i>mandatory </i></b>when there are Exalts for which it will be irrelevant? &quot; That's what I'm criticizing. Not the existence of culture or aesthetics --- but making something mandatory. Every other splat has both ronin/outcaste/rebel/etc AND multiple sub-variants to pick-and-choose from (making them all super cool).<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;these are things I can pick-and-choose from to inspire my Lunar&quot; is one thing.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;these are things all Lunars must have in common, and hey yo, I'm throwing a bonfire moon-gazing orgy next week and us Lunars thought you'd like to come along.... oh wait, I thought I recognized your Tell.... you mean you DON'T have cat ears?&quot; is something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","user":"RedRiotousRam","date":". 01-27-2015, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:43:42-08:00","id":383330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383255#post383255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have vaguely had a point in the other stuff, insofar as the possibility of references to figures like Ivan the Terrible or Josef Stalin who were probably genuinely mentally ill, but I think your last point is begging the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean? I might just be reading your post wrong. Ma-Ha-Suchi is a pretty good analog for Ivan the Terrible of Josef Stalin so why wouldn't it be possible for him to have a mental illness driving his actions too?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:52:59-08:00","id":383335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383330#post383330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean? I might just be reading your post wrong. Ma-Ha-Suchi is a pretty good analog for Ivan the Terrible of Josef Stalin so why wouldn't it be possible for him to have a mental illness driving his actions too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because I was using a Chimera (with goat and wolf mixture) to give an example of character growth resulting in changing totems. The gist was:<br /> <br /> Lunar with passive/patient/herbivore animal totem -- over decades of warfare -- acquires an aggressive/predatory/pack-hunter totem, as she grows into a stronger, harsher leader.<br /> <br /> Lunar with an aggressive/predatory/pack-hunter -- over decades, reflecting on the tragedies brought by her war-mongering -- acquires a passive/patient/herbivore totem, as her connection strengthens to more nurturing creatures.<br /> <br /> He used a straw man (against this defense of Chimera), saying the example is bad because &quot;lulwut Ma-Ha-Suchi crazy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:59:33-08:00","id":383358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383330#post383330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean? I might just be reading your post wrong. Ma-Ha-Suchi is a pretty good analog for Ivan the Terrible of Josef Stalin so why wouldn't it be possible for him to have a mental illness driving his actions too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, because we know Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't have a mental illness! I mean, Vance just said earlier in this very thread that he absolutely does not have a mental illness. I'm not sure why you'd bother debating something you positively know is not a thing. Maybe I missed something though.<br /> <br /> We're straying off topic though. I'm curious what everyone thinks of this new &quot;dominion&quot; mechanic. I know we don't know much about it, but it seems like it allows a Lunar to claim territory. I'm just curious what all this entails. Does the Lunar have some control over the territory, or does it maybe act kinda like a manse by bolstering the Lunar while he's within his area of influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-27-2015, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T11:03:32-08:00","id":383359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383130#post383130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As grotesque as this might be, I've always interpreted Ma Ha Suchi as a satyr like being, with all the hedonism it entails, corrupted into a Baphomet &quot;satanic&quot; symbol of the beast kind of figure. He's certainly mad over the events of the Usurpation, and has consolidated his power, raided nearby settlements and made an army of Beastmen, both powerful and perverse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I really like this interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T11:18:29-08:00","id":383366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383358#post383358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm, because we know Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't have a mental illness! I mean, Vance just said earlier in this very post that he absolutely does not have a mental illness. I'm not sure why you'd bother debating something you positively know is not a thing. Maybe I missed something though.</div> </div> </div> </div>People aren't just spontaneously evil warmongers, there is always an underlying psychological reason for brutal and evil actions, whether it be addiction, psychopathy, post traumatic stress, or some other factor. The actions of Ma-Ha-Suchi are not those of a well adjusted person, they are unhealthy and uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> <b>If he does not have some major psychological disorder or mental illness I would really like to know how else you can possibly explain his behavior?</b><br /> <br /> Vance makes an important point that we should not vilify all mental illness, that doesn't mean that mental illness can NEVER be a source of villainy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T11:29:12-08:00","id":383383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383366#post383366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People aren't just spontaneously evil warmongers, there is always an underlying psychological reason for brutal and evil actions, whether it be addiction, psychopathy, post traumatic stress, or some other factor. The actions of Ma-Ha-Suchi are not those of a well adjusted person, they are unhealthy and uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> <b>If he does not have some major psychological disorder or mental illness I would really like to know how else you can possibly explain his behavior?</b><br /> <br /> Vance makes an important point that we should not vilify all mental illness, that doesn't mean that mental illness can NEVER be a source of villainy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you have confirmation from a Dev that it is NOT a mental illness that drives Ma-Ha-Suchi. Also their are plenty of people who have done horrible things in our own history, yet they did it for what they felt was justifiable means. Whether you think those reasons are justifiable or not isn't the issue. As for Exalted, pure evil is very real. Also do remember that while Suchi doesn't have a mental illness, he is very old and the Great Curse has had a very long time to warp his outlook on life. If you really need a reason right now to explain his behavior... the Great Curse is your reason. It's a safe bet that it's at least partly to blame even if it isn't the sole reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T11:30:49-08:00","id":383384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383366#post383366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People aren't just spontaneously evil warmongers, there is always an underlying psychological reason for brutal and evil actions, whether it be addiction, psychopathy, post traumatic stress, or some other factor. The actions of Ma-Ha-Suchi are not those of a well adjusted person, they are unhealthy and uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> <b>If he does not have some major psychological disorder or mental illness I would really like to know how else you can possibly explain his behavior?</b><br /> <br /> Vance makes an important point that we should not vilify all mental illness, that doesn't mean that mental illness can NEVER be a source of villainy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted probably won't be presenting it as mental illness, but the Usurpation is a big-enough event (read:life-, identity- and world-shattering) to cause all sorts of disorders, up to and including PTSD, Dissociative Personality and many, many others. On top of that, hiding from the post-usurpation death-squads, living through the Contageon and Crusade... hoooo boy, Things can get bad.<br /> <br /> In a world where such disorders aren't necessarily even recognized, much less treated, stretched over thousands of years.... yeah. Things get <i>really, reeaally</i> bad. The kind of person one needs to become to <i>survive</i> all of that, even - or especially - as an exalted isn't someone the returning Solars would want to keep around, mostly because they don't know any better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:03:58-08:00","id":383397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383383#post383383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you have confirmation from a Dev that it is NOT a mental illness that drives Ma-Ha-Suchi. Also their are plenty of people who have done horrible things in our own history, yet they did it for what they felt was justifiable means. Whether you think those reasons are justifiable or not isn't the issue. As for Exalted, pure evil is very real. Also do remember that while Suchi doesn't have a mental illness, he is very old and the Great Curse has had a very long time to warp his outlook on life. If you really need a reason right now to explain his behavior... the Great Curse is your reason. It's a safe bet that it's at least partly to blame even if it isn't the sole reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrary to the forum's genral opinion I am allowed to think a Dev is wrong if the facts I see suggest they are!<br /> <br /> People can do evil things without being mentally ill, but usually under some social or religious pressure (thinks Nazi Youth and the Crusades), Ma-Ha-Suchi's actions aren't driven by either of these things as far as I can tell, he solely operates on his own motivations. Maybe it is the great curse that makes him behave the way he does, but I would also argue that the Great Curse itself essentially functions as a mental illness causing individuals to act outside of normal healthy psychological patterns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:23:57-08:00","id":383426,"title":"","content":"What's this tangent about mental illness and warfare? Dude's perfectly rational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People aren't just spontaneously evil warmongers, there is always an underlying psychological reason for brutal and evil actions, whether it be addiction, psychopathy, post traumatic stress, or some other factor. The actions of Ma-Ha-Suchi are not those of a well adjusted person, they are unhealthy and uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> <b>If he does not have some major psychological disorder or mental illness I would really like to know how else you can possibly explain his behavior?</b> </div> </div> </div><b>What is evil about warmongering?</b><br /> <br /> The man has the strength of his convictions (a Virtue in this game). And he has the long-vision to see that people will die (sooner or later) -- so better to cull them now than to massacre ten times as many later. Why is lazy live-and-let-live pacifism always glorified? It's monstrous. And boring. This game is supposed to be full of <i>exciting</i> people living in <i>interesting</i> times.<br /> <br /> There are perfectly sane and functional people --- who will murder to defend their country; who will murder in show of loyalty to their god and faith; who will clear cut rival peoples just to preserve their own. Now think of old people, especially veterans who remain resentful and racist against whoever they fought decades ago. Now make him a half-beast Exalted god-king. Why <u>shouldn't</u> he want to murder his way across civilization out of bitterness? He's human.<br /> <br /> Or as a wise man just said...<br /> &quot;Also their are plenty of people who have done horrible things in our own history, yet they did it for what they felt was justifiable means. Whether you think those reasons are justifiable or not isn't the issue.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Exalted, pure evil is very real. </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be crazy to be harmful.<br /> You don't need to be unreasonably malevolent either.<br /> <br /> As you say --- there are many who do horrible things because they felt it was justifiable or necessary.<br /> <br /> And I'd argue even the Yozis and Neverborn aren't truly &quot;evil&quot; in so far as they're adhering to their nature (and asking the Ebon Dragon to be virtuous is as impossible as asking Light to be Dark).<br /> <br /> I'm queasy with &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; -- they're gross and nebulous terms, D&amp;D can keep that claptrap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:38:18-08:00","id":383433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383366#post383366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actions of Ma-Ha-Suchi are not those of a well adjusted person, they are unhealthy and uncontrolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be suffering from the delusion that anyone who is not well-adjusted is necessarily suffering from a mental condition. As someone who is not well-adjusted, I find that offensive.<br /> <br /> Mankind often takes actions that are unhealthy and uncontrolled. Look at tobacco sales figures. Look at all the abusive relationships, the co-dependent behaviors, the crime statistics. Look at the news. Plenty of people choose to let their emotions control what they do, often because they think they can get away with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:51:30-08:00","id":383463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383433#post383433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be suffering from the delusion that anyone who is not well-adjusted is necessarily suffering from a mental condition. As someone who is not well-adjusted, I find that offensive.<br /> <br /> Mankind often takes actions that are unhealthy and uncontrolled. Look at tobacco sales figures. Look at all the abusive relationships, the co-dependent behaviors, the crime statistics. Look at the news. Plenty of people choose to let their emotions control what they do, often because they think they can get away with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people consider addiction to be a mental illness, the chemistry of your brain has been physically altered to cause habitual behavior often beyond your ability to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:00:30-08:00","id":383469,"title":"","content":"O_o<br /> <br /> Sooooo...um...getting away from the mental illness chat for a bit, I personally prefer Ma-Ha-Suchi's transformation as something he did to <i>himself</i>, to demonstrate his resolve and get the rest of the Lunar survivors of the Usurpation to take him seriously after several centuries spent carefully-cultivating a persona as someone who's never taken seriously. Less Seth Brundle from <i>The Fly</i>, more Keyser Soze from <i>The Usual Suspects</i>. In this interpretation, he's still a monster, but at least an <i>interesting </i>kind of monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:08:28-08:00","id":383478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383469#post383469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O_o<br /> <br /> Sooooo...um...getting away from the mental illness chat for a bit, I personally prefer Ma-Ha-Suchi's transformation as something he did to <i>himself</i>, to demonstrate his resolve and get the rest of the Lunar survivors of the Usurpation to take him seriously after several centuries spent carefully-cultivating a persona as someone who's never taken seriously. Less Seth Brundle from <i>The Fly</i>, more Keyser Soze from <i>The Usual Suspects</i>. In this interpretation, he's still a monster, but at least an <i>interesting </i>kind of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What would his motivation for making this change be other than good old despotic power? He seemed like he was pretty content with the pleasure of the first age, so what is stopping him from seeking those same pleasures in the age of sorrows? It's a interesting thought!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:22:51-08:00","id":383514,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit late to this subject, but I personally am among those who really don't like the moonsilver tattoos. Why? Because I'm not a tattoo person. I would find it totally awesome if my Lunars didn't have to have their skin marred by tattoos in order to function as Lunars. Barring that, it'd be nice to be able to obfuscate the tattoos with minimal effort.<br /> <br /> As for Ma-Ha-Suchi, I can easily see him as believing himself to be a righteous rebel set out to crush a usurping corrupt dictatorship. No mental illness required. Unless you consider being an Exalt to be an illness in that one would rather make history than have history... uh... made onto... him? I dunno. I kind of lost the train of thought there, but my point is that he's a demigod who hates the Empire, so building up an army built around its destruction seems pretty much normal. Maybe he hates too much... probably he does. However, one has to realize that not all aberrant behavior should be grounds for classification of illness.<br /> <br /> And finally! On the subject of Chimeras... is it true that most people play Chimeras as mindless murder-machines? That seems rather strange to me, even as one who learned Exalted from Second Edition. Every Chimera is a hero who has essentially been lost to their most defining urges as well as lost their form, but that hardly means that all they do is murder everything all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:54:56-08:00","id":383551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383478#post383478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would his motivation for making this change be other than good old despotic power? He seemed like he was pretty content with the pleasure of the first age, so what is stopping him from seeking those same pleasures in the age of sorrows? It's a interesting thought!</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine in part because the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded expelled him and all other Lunars (where they didn't manage to kill said Lunars) to the outskirts of Creation in a violent coup and then set up a widespread religion and world-straddling colossus of an empire with killing or otherwise keeping them relegated to the sidelines very high on the list of priorities. Also, the First Age is not the Second: the full heights of pleasures he may have enjoyed in the former are no longer nearly so easily obtained in the latter, if available at all. Someone who'd grown intimately accustomed to the lap of First Age luxury could regard the what's possible with Second Age luxury as a pale, unsatisfying shadow.<br /> <br /> Also also -- and putting entirely aside that someone who's been violently driven from his comfortable home context and known the death or suffering of huge swaths of people he cared about is <i>prrrrrrobably</i> gonna hold a teensy bit of resentment, never mind some concern about it happening again if he doesn't take corrective action -- the previously mentioned world-straddling colossus of an empire (still very happy to kill him) is seizing all of the desirable resources it can to prop itself up and provide the highest pleasures of the Second Age to its scions. So, if asked why he is waging war against the Realm instead of just &quot;enjoying the pleasures of the Second Age,&quot; should he answer at all, he may angrily snarl, &quot;What do you think I'm <i>trying</i> to do!?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383514#post383514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally! On the subject of Chimeras... is it true that most people play Chimeras as mindless murder-machines? That seems rather strange to me, even as one who learned Exalted from Second Edition. Every Chimera is a hero who has essentially been lost to their most defining urges as well as lost their form, but that hardly means that all they do is murder everything all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm away from my books, but I believe things are more severe than you recall. Every Chimera ultimately gets its Motivation replaced with &quot;Survive,&quot; for one thing, and I'm pretty sure that's not the last of the worrisome changes. It's not just a matter of being &quot;no true form, constant/super-easy Limit Break.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tidying up a few pronouns and a bit of phrasing. Added an extra sentence or two in elaboration. 01-27-2015, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:49:05-08:00","id":383615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he does not have some major psychological disorder or mental illness I would really like to know how else you can possibly explain his behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div> Cultural values that differ from your own. Also, not all forms of delusion are mental illness, and most colloqial references to &quot;paranoia&quot; are not. A figure like Ma-Ha-Suchi <i>could</i> be mentally ill in the same manner Stalin might have been, but your assertion that he <i>must</i> be is faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:54:18-08:00","id":383618,"title":"","content":"In any case, while there are historical examples of tyrants who were mentally ill, it's not really necessary to make them especially prominent in Exalted, for the aforementioned reason that ham-handed associations between mental illness and moral atrocity are already overly abundant and disgusting. The hurtfullness of how the idea has been used in the past is enough to make it worth fading into the background for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:59:03-08:00","id":383621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383469#post383469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O_o<br /> <br /> Sooooo...um...getting away from the mental illness chat for a bit, I personally prefer Ma-Ha-Suchi's transformation as something he did to <i>himself</i>, to demonstrate his resolve and get the rest of the Lunar survivors of the Usurpation to take him seriously after several centuries spent carefully-cultivating a persona as someone who's never taken seriously. Less Seth Brundle from <i>The Fly</i>, more Keyser Soze from <i>The Usual Suspects</i>. In this interpretation, he's still a monster, but at least an <i>interesting </i>kind of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have a lot of 2e lore holding you back. Just as surely as the Ebon Dragon isn't going to be a creature of anti-Virtue in EX3, it's highly unlikely that they're going to keep MHS's background from DotFA and Lunars 2e, especially since everything from DotFA is going to be scrapped and Lunars 2e made Holden swear a blue streak on the forums some four years ago or so with its characterization problems.<br /> <br /> What MHS thinks is probably going to be a slightly modified form of what you got in his E:tL description. Rather than hating on all civilization, he specifically wants to water the fields of the Blessed Isle with the blood of the Terrestrials and all of their supporters, right down to the last frightful peasant, because they're all complicit in the evil that is the so-called Realm of the Scarlet Dynasty. Unfortunately, he doesn't really trust the Threshold states neighboring his Nameless Lair to resist the plague of the Dynasty on their own, and so is looking to set up shop first in the River Province and then overflow into other regions. While this could be beneficial in some respects - he's not about to let the Mask of Winters stay in the lands of the living - it's more likely to involve the entirety of the Scavenger Lands that remains alive being pressed into service in a military training regimen that makes Lookshy seem small and subdued, with the veneration of Luna set up at the head of everyone's temple and all other deities put behind her. Everyone is going to learn how to hunt, and they'll sacrifice any dissenters to the Bloody Huntress at the behest of Her intermediary, the Prince of the Northern Jungle.<br /> <br /> If you have access to a copy of Exalted: the Lunars, just read &quot;the 'Realm' of the Scarlet Dynasty, if you can even call it that&quot; whenever E:tL uses the word &quot;civilization&quot;, &quot;weak settled folk&quot;, and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:01:33-08:00","id":383627,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In First Edition, they played up the Barbarian savage part a lot --- but akin to Solars, Terrestrial Lost Eggs, etc, it wasn't absurd to imagine a Lunar who shunned his peers, stuck to the cities, did their own thing. </div> </div> </div>Luna would take your exaltation back if you got too soft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:22:46-08:00","id":383653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383551#post383551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm away from my books, but I believe things are more severe than you to recall. Every Chimera ultimately gets its Motivation replaced with &quot;Survive,&quot; for one thing, and I'm pretty sure that's not the last of the worrisome changes. It's not just a matter of being &quot;no true form, constant/super-easy Limit Break.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I, likewise, am not near my book, but I believe that those are really the only three things that chimeras are saddled with. Now, being in constant limit break forever means that they're certainly not going to be terribly rational, but unless every chimera has the &quot;murder everyone that they see&quot; limit, it doesn't preclude them from still being characters.<br /> <br /> Granted, the only thing that chimeras were ever shown as being were mindless monsters in second edition, so that certainly helps color people's opinions of them. Still, if a chimera had the Curse of the Mother Hen limit break, she'd be a ridiculously protective being of constant mutations bent on her own survival. Certainly something different than the beast that just eats everything.<br /> <br /> I once ran a story that the players particularly enjoyed, about a chimera that had been haunting a shadowland for centuries. Originally the shadowland was something like a mental institution that had been appropriated by a scholar who tortured inmates in order to purposefully shadowland the place, then he studied the effects of the underworld on the minds of the insane. The Chimera in question was once an inmate there who Exalted and escaped, then returned years later already twisted. Using chimera charms, she killed everyone there, then spend the next two centuries endlessly rebirthing and hunting down the administrators who tortured her and the other inmates. Her limit break was the Curse of the Drunken Monkey, and endlessly murdering the people who she hated so much was one of the most enjoyable things she could think of. There was more of course, involving her chimeric beastman children, a nearby town that the chimera had terrorized into a stockholm syndrome type scenario, and a hekatonkhire that sang a song of cannibalism, but the important thing was that the chimera was an actual character instead of a mindless monster.<br /> <br /> That's not to imply that she wasn't an antagonist of course, she totally was. So... my point is that chimeras can be fun! Even the second edition types!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:40:19-08:00","id":383687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383551#post383551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine in part because the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded expelled him and all other Lunars to the outskirts of Creation in a violent coup and then set up a widespread religion and world-straddling colossus of an empire with killing or otherwise keeping them relegated to the sidelines very high on the list of priorities. Also, the First Age is not the Second: the full heights of pleasures he may have enjoyed in the former are no longer nearly so easily obtained in the latter, if available at all.<br /> <br /> Also also -- and putting entirely aside that someone who's been violently driven from his comfortable home context and known the death or suffering of huge swaths of people one probably have cared about is <i>prrrrrrobably</i> gonna hold a teensy bit of resentment, never mind some concern about it happening again if one doesn't take great efforts to discourage such -- the previously mentioned world-straddling colossus of an empire that would be very happy to kill him is seizing all of the desirable resources it can to prop itself up and provide the highest pleasures of the Second Age to its scions. So, if asked why he is waging war against the Realm instead of just enjoying the pleasures of the Second Age, if he answers at all, he's likely to angrily snarl, &quot;What do you think I'm <i>trying</i> to do!?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this you could almost characterize him like Kublai Kahn living in Xanadu with all the comforts you could possibly imagine...but it's not enough, he can see those Chinese to the south and they have such beautiful things, such a refined culture, IT MUST BE HIS!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T15:46:27-08:00","id":383700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383653#post383653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, likewise, am not near my book, but I believe that those are really the only three things that chimeras are saddled with. Now, being in constant limit break forever means that they're certainly not going to be terribly rational, but unless every chimera has the &quot;murder everyone that they see&quot; limit, it doesn't preclude them from still being characters.<br /> <br /> Granted, the only thing that chimeras were ever shown as being were mindless monsters in second edition, so that certainly helps color people's opinions of them. Still, if a chimera had the Curse of the Mother Hen limit break, she'd be a ridiculously protective being of constant mutations bent on her own survival. Certainly something different than the beast that just eats everything.<br /> <br /> I once ran a story that the players particularly enjoyed, about a chimera that had been haunting a shadowland for centuries. Originally the shadowland was something like a mental institution that had been appropriated by a scholar who tortured inmates in order to purposefully shadowland the place, then he studied the effects of the underworld on the minds of the insane. The Chimera in question was once an inmate there who Exalted and escaped, then returned years later already twisted. Using chimera charms, she killed everyone there, then spend the next two centuries endlessly rebirthing and hunting down the administrators who tortured her and the other inmates. Her limit break was the Curse of the Drunken Monkey, and endlessly murdering the people who she hated so much was one of the most enjoyable things she could think of. There was more of course, involving her chimeric beastman children, a nearby town that the chimera had terrorized into a stockholm syndrome type scenario, and a hekatonkhire that sang a song of cannibalism, but the important thing was that the chimera was an actual character instead of a mindless monster.<br /> <br /> That's not to imply that she wasn't an antagonist of course, she totally was. So... my point is that chimeras can be fun! Even the second edition types!</div> </div> </div> </div>This really appeals to me, Chimera as monsters barely hanging on to a scrap of their human motivation, like Clayface from Batman, or Envy from FMA. I like having true monsters who also have some sliver of motivation beyond &quot;eat all the villagers!&quot;<br /> <br /> (As a random aside, are there stats for Hecatonchires in 2e? That's another monster I would like to look at.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:25:37-08:00","id":383764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383700#post383700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really appeals to me, Chimera as monsters barely hanging on to a scrap of their human motivation, like Clayface from Batman, or Envy from FMA. I like having true monsters who also have some sliver of motivation beyond &quot;eat all the villagers!&quot;<br /> <br /> (As a random aside, are there stats for Hecatonchires in 2e? That's another monster I would like to look at.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are stats for at least one Hekatonkhire in... either Abyssals, or the Black Treatise. Each one is entirely unique though. They can be as different from one another as Juggernaught is from Mother Bog is from Vorvin-Derlin is from Mount Mostath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:28:39-08:00","id":383781,"title":"","content":"A few Hekatonkhires are statted up, but there's no base Hekatonkhire frame to build off of or anything. The one I made was initially inspired by Soul Reaver's Zephon and a bit the Red Queen from American Macgee's Alice. It ended up not being too similar to either of them other than some aesthetics. The Hekatonkhire, Voiceless Singer of Desperate Hunger, was a subterranean being that sang an inaudible song that inspired cannibalism. People would start seeing other people as suitable food choices, but after over a century even the trees were devouring one-another (very slowly) and the buildings in the area as well. When a cannibal or someone who was cannibalized died, the Hekatonkhire would snare their soul and spin it into soulsteel wire with which it would create items of beauty. It was composed of stone tentacles as large as trees that permeated the shadowland centered on the House of Rightful Thought (the sanitarium), and when it wished to address others the tentacles would bleed Old Realm script (it didn't talk, as it had no voice). For an ancient death behemoth it was actually quite reasonable and had no interest in fighting. It only wished to sing and was unhappy when the player characters killed its muse (the chimera).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:38:21-08:00","id":383793,"title":"","content":"Recently, my brother wrote a review of The Iron Giant which articulated a very good point quite well; the villain in that movie is not in the least bit sympathetic, and he's actually pretty terrible, but he has a clear and personal motivation which escalates the degree of danger he represents logically. He is not a monster, he is not insane, and while his cultural milieu informs his actions his own person takes them several steps beyond, and he almost led to the deaths of at least several thousand people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T17:19:21-08:00","id":383832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383793#post383793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently, my brother wrote a review of The Iron Giant which articulated a very good point quite well; the villain in that movie is not in the least bit sympathetic, and he's actually pretty terrible, but he has a clear and personal motivation which escalates the degree of danger he represents logically. He is not a monster, he is not insane, and while his cultural milieu informs his actions his own person takes them several steps beyond, and he almost led to the deaths of at least several thousand people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I remember that movie. That guy is really a great example of how you shouldn't automatically assume malevolence, sometimes people just do stupid **** because they didn't take the time to think things through to their logical conclusion. I mean, it is pretty hard to top a guy who calls a nuclear strike down on something and doesn't consider the fact that they are standing right next to said thing until someone says (paraphrased) 'guess who is at ground zero, agent dipshit?'<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T18:31:58-08:00","id":383866,"title":"","content":"I look forward to seeing what 3e will churn out for Lunars and their controlled areas. I'm digging the Conrad Heart of Darkness vibe that (may be?) going on, and am hella interested in animal shapes as viable . . Err, power expressions.<br /> <br /> Although, I am kinda sad to see that Lunar Coyote, Ansani, Fox Spirit and Grandfather Mantis aren't so much a supported Lunar concept. Maybe they make better gods/Raksha/elementals/etc anyway... *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T19:27:27-08:00","id":383896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383866#post383866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, I am kinda sad to see that Lunar Coyote, Ansani, Fox Spirit and Grandfather Mantis aren't so much a supported Lunar concept. Maybe they make better gods/Raksha/elementals/etc anyway... *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>Anansi isn't an illusionist, he's a trickster. He doesn't need bullshit illusions to pull tricks on someone. Quite often you can get by on being a <i>really</i> sly bastard who's good at talking one thing up, and another thing down.<br /> <br /> If you require the usage of <i>silent image</i> to get someone to attack a tar man, you're not trickstering hard enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-27-2015, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:56:00-08:00","id":383949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383896#post383896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anansi isn't an illusionist, he's a trickster. He doesn't need bullshit illusions to pull tricks on someone. Quite often you can get by on being a <i>really</i> sly bastard who's good at talking one thing up, and another thing down.<br /> <br /> If you require the usage of <i>silent image</i> to get someone to attack a tar man, you're not trickstering hard enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is an excellent point. I guess what's bothering me more is the (indescribable, not sure if really there) <i>feeling</i> that I'm losing the idea of trickster Lunars, or really any Exalted that expressed the sort of myth stories that one might outside of Greek/European fantasy and Asian political-fantasy epics.<br /> <br /> It is possible, however, that I'm just giving &quot;Illusions&quot; more breadth in this context than it deserves. If I can still do (or more accurately, properly do) trickster Lunar in 3rd Edition I will be quite happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:06:46-08:00","id":383956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is an excellent point. I guess what's bothering me more is the (indescribable, not sure if really there) <i>feeling</i> that I'm losing the idea of trickster Lunars, or really any Exalted that expressed the sort of myth stories that one might outside of Greek/European fantasy and Asian political-fantasy epics. </div> </div> </div>If Ex3: Lunar won't be the trickster splat, then we can always use the superior version in Ex1 and Ex2 ~ &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T02:35:07-08:00","id":384067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383832#post383832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That guy is really a great example of how you shouldn't automatically assume malevolence</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about malevolent, but he was undeniably a jackass from the very outset.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:46:05-08:00","id":384376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383949#post383949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an excellent point. I guess what's bothering me more is the (indescribable, not sure if really there) <i>feeling</i> that I'm losing the idea of trickster Lunars, or really any Exalted that expressed the sort of myth stories that one might outside of Greek/European fantasy and Asian political-fantasy epics.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, we've been <i>told</i> that &quot;trickster&quot; is very much an intended role for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=383949#post383949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible, however, that I'm just giving &quot;Illusions&quot; more breadth in this context than it deserves. If I can still do (or more accurately, properly do) trickster Lunar in 3rd Edition I will be quite happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess this depends on what you think you need to do to &quot;properly do trickster Lunar.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T12:38:02-08:00","id":384423,"title":"","content":"Human history is full of trickters.<br /> <br /> If you can only be a trickster with GODLIKE AMAZING POWER, then you're probably not clever enough to be a trickster.<br /> <br /> Same goes for all other categories. Believe it or not, there have been epic orators, warriors, sages, etc without magic (such that in some cases, magic was later ascribed).<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> Someone who enjoys playing manipulative bastards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T13:02:18-08:00","id":384434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384423#post384423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human history is full of trickters.<br /> <br /> If you can only be a trickster with GODLIKE AMAZING POWER, then you're probably not clever enough to be a trickster.<br /> <br /> Same goes for all other categories. Believe it or not, there have been epic orators, warriors, sages, etc without magic (such that in some cases, magic was later ascribed).<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> Someone who enjoys playing manipulative bastards</div> </div> </div> </div>And certainly this is so. I think the crux of it is more when a splat has it suggested as prominently as Lunars do, there are certain expectations. People can do tricksters in any splat, but want to find more magic in the splat that's especially useful for someone who's keen on trickster-y stuff. People want more capabilities that really lend themselves to and encourage such a play style.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is also the splat that has as a baseline power an ability that makes it really easy to trick others into thinking one is an animal. And a likely low-hanging (if not also baseline) power that makes it really easy to trick others into thinking one is a different person than one is. So... Depending on how seeing through Lunar transformations works out in EX3, those'd already be some fairly potent options in their tricksters' tool kits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T13:08:23-08:00","id":384459,"title":"","content":"I'd rather they give lunars a good solid theme then try to incorporate everything 2E said lunars were and them end up an incoherent mess again. There are still unrevealed exalt types so perhaps one of them will get some of the concepts lunars are shedding like being tricky exalts tied to the wyld with the ability to sort of distort Creation and do things like make pocket dimensions and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T13:31:54-08:00","id":384469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384459#post384459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather they give lunars a good solid theme then try to incorporate everything 2E said lunars were and them end up an incoherent mess again. There are still unrevealed exalt types so perhaps one of them will get some of the concepts lunars are shedding like being tricky exalts tied to the wyld with the ability to sort of distort Creation and do things like make pocket dimensions and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we disagree on the big picture. If Lunars no longer have any real trickster elements to them, I imagine they won't be billed as tricksters anymore. That'll be the incongruity resolved.<br /> EDIT: I mean, I'll be disappointed if &quot;no real trickster elements&quot; is a thing, as that always seemed like such a rich area, and was one of the big draws to the splat for me. But I at least expect the devs will be forthright about that if it becomes the direction they're going (with the caveat that different people may be thinking of different things when they say and hear, &quot;trickster&quot; ).<br /> <br /> I'll note that from what they've said are on the outs, though, &quot;trickster&quot; isn't necessarily one of the things they're ditching.* While it's been a while since we had such a statement, and the context was admittedly not gunning for it in particular, we've had this statement since Holden's giant barbarian post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are, however, intended to partake of stylistic barbarism-- they're designed for it from the ground up and many of their problems in Second Edition came from a deliberate attempt to reject this, I think as a result of conflating it with the other two kinds of barbarism. The fact of the matter is, to the degree that the Exalted splats echo other source material, Lunars are werewolves, tribal legends, and pagan culture-heroes. They're supposed to look rough-edged compared to the more refined Solars; their Attribute magic is supposed to look raw and powerful compared to the deft, polished sheen of Ability magic; their shapeshifting points to a primal font of imagery and aptitude-- their archetypes are &quot;warrior, trickster, shaman.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>* Distorting Creation and illusions are indeed straight-up not in their bag of tricks, per John's remarks. As such, Lunar tricksters would be executing the idea in a different fashion than, say, the Fair Folk would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Clarifying edit. 01-28-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:09:41-08:00","id":384535,"title":"","content":"Lunars without at least some expressions of being tricksters are not the Chosen of the god who was written up in Glories of the Most High.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:23:21-08:00","id":384543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384535#post384535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars without at least some expressions of being tricksters are not the Chosen of the god who was written up in Glories of the Most High.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gods that were written up in Glories of the Most High should never eat up that much word count again. Aren't the devs on record that they think Glories was a bad idea for the line in the long run, due to the over-focus on the Incarnae as informing the nature of the Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:54:20-08:00","id":384578,"title":"","content":"Irrelevant; the Luna written up there is still our blueprint for the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:59:53-08:00","id":384582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384578#post384578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irrelevant; the Luna written up there is still our blueprint for the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would 2E Luna matter to 3E lunars anymore then 1E 'I'm going to revoke your exaltation if you aren't hardcore enough' Luna does to 2nd edition lunars?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T16:31:00-08:00","id":384596,"title":"","content":"Did the five Lunar Castes in the First Age correlate to her main personas, Bloody Huntress, Silver Horned Watcher, Two-Faced Bride, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:05:26-08:00","id":384914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384582#post384582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would 2E Luna matter to 3E lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Second Edition Luna is great, and the developers have frequently stated that she's the guidepost for what good Lunars look like.<br /> <br /> Really, even in the context of Glories and possibilities of over focusing on the Incarnae, Luna is done fairly well; it mostly describes the mythology of her and alludes to her power and personality, without going into much focus on anything like specific aspirations or areas of interest. Take out all of the entourage and mechanics stuff, pare down the description of the aspects, and distil the rest, and you could get a good three or so paragraphs of evocative but offhand description to go in a Games of Divinity style basic outline of the Incarnae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the five Lunar Castes in the First Age correlate to her main personas, Bloody Huntress, Silver Horned Watcher, Two-Faced Bride, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall them once alluding to the idea that, while the mythology of the Othermoons, including ones who left particular marks, is good for figuring out Luna and Lunars, the aspects aren't really something they're interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-29-2015, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T06:08:01-08:00","id":384935,"title":"","content":"Second Edition Luna was <u>fantastic</u>. I loved her every bit as much as I hate the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> Luna was <u>glorious</u>. Her aspects were varied such that her beastial side was only a fragment of the whole ; such that rather than 1 psuedo-monolithic &quot;culture&quot;, we had 10 or 11 or so archetypes from which to &quot;validate&quot; our concepts, depending on which one we might emulate. She was a huntress and a seducer, not an animal guarding territory but a witch beckoning the very waves and storms with her allure. Many of the charms in that book became my favorites (be it customizing offspring or almost all the No Moon charms). Glories of Luna made me want play Lunars (and without exaggeration, when I did role another Lunar, I used that book (including its charms) more than the actual Lunar book.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact is a flat faux-culture emulating WtA with a tiny fraction of the population (300 or less god-kings scattered on the extreme and opposite ends of Creation -- not an entire species of Beastman-like werewolf tribes). And the way it was written, some STs could (and would) use it like a mallet to smack you over the head, since one way or another you were expected to leave home and join them ; do their silly shamanistic rites ; embrace the tattooed deformity they pushed with their kool-aid ; and then owe them for it. Only Lunars &amp; Sidereal Exalted have to worry about ancient 1st Age Elders who could easily show up to curbstomp you into line --- and only Lunars had the numbers and culture that encouraged conformity to a bunch of furries.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Much as the Abyssal Exalted have their Deathlords (and a few cities in Shadowlands), Infernals have their Yozis (and a few unique cities in Creation), Dragon-Blooded have Houses and Gens, Sidereals have their Bureaus ---- I'd nosebleed if Lunars had something as varied and rich as Luna's aspects as inspiration (such that if they have a sense of &quot;cultural kinship&quot;, it be one that fosters and embraces their diversity). I loved that the charms in that book also drew upon some of those aspects (World-Walkers and Mother-of-Monsters in particular).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T07:24:38-08:00","id":385013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384578#post384578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irrelevant; the Luna written up there is still our blueprint for the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. Isn't it relevant though? I mean, why state that less word count should be spent on describing Incarna otherwise? Do you really think such a statement would be meant to be interpreted as, &quot;we don't want to spend that kind of word count because it's already been spent? So just go look at 2e's write up for more info&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because I'd interpret it more as, &quot;spending that much word count and providing that level of detail on Incarna makes them too mundane, and since we want the to be less mundane-- and we have the opportunity, with a new edition, to start fresh-- you should all ignore what came before, and we will say less going forward.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T07:26:29-08:00","id":385015,"title":"","content":"You know, the talk of Lunars as Folk Heroes makes me think of folk tales like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chasse-galerie\" target=\"_blank\">La Chasse-Galerie</a> or whatnot, where Lunars are a bunch of Quebeckers sitting down in the woods in the dead of winter to have a beer and talk about their wives and hockey. They just happen to also be werewolves and runs-faster-than-a-speeding-train local celebrities. (With thick Joual or Acadian accents no less)<br /> <br /> Edit: oh void, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cood3ZnRJk8\" target=\"_blank\">Elvis Gratton</a> as a Folk Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-29-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T07:31:14-08:00","id":385018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385013#post385013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'd interpret it more as, &quot;spending that much word count and providing that level of detail on Incarna makes them too mundane, and since we want the to be less mundane-- and we have the opportunity, with a new edition, to start fresh-- you should all ignore what came before, and we will say less going forward.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-Glories, Luna seemed Mundane. Lack of detail doesn't automatically make one mysterious or fantastic --- it can also just result in &quot;this NPC is not used at all&quot; or &quot;the ST defaults to the most generic, average idea they have&quot; or &quot;the ST copies some other lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> Infernals are a good comparison. I <u>loved</u> them as a concept since 1E -- but we never got a write-up so I never saw an ST use them (unless it was as super-Satanic antagonists in the most cliche villain roles ever).<br /> <br /> So<br /> <br /> The theory doesn't amount to practice.<br /> <br /> And as aforementioned, Glories of Luna revitalized the splat for me (such that I was able to get concepts approved that - going just off the Lunar book - STs previously thought were too weird). Her aspects added the kind of rich yet different <b>archetypes </b>that Great Houses and Deathlords and Yozis provide everyone else with (validating more eccentric interpretations than --- what I feel --- the homogenizing Silver Pact mish-mash gave us). The word count spent on her only <i>enriched</i> Lunars, validating those who didn't want to be the 235th &quot;generic glorified beastman trickster-warrior in silver ink&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","user":"RedRiotousRam","date":". 01-29-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:16:52-08:00","id":385044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384935#post384935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Edition Luna was <u>fantastic</u>. I loved her every bit as much as I hate the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the <i>idea</i> of a Silver Pact, especially as an institution for preserving whatever's left of Creation's glorious (or occasionally deeply-horrific) past, but loathe the execution. I'd prefer to see it as a sort of loosely-affiliated support network that depends on individual initiative for starting projects but a Lunar can try to get support by selling other Lunars on the plan. Super Secret-Handshake Awesome Abduction Club for Failures can DIAF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:19:41-08:00","id":385045,"title":"","content":"In regards to Luna, whatever else, I do NOT want wordcount spent detailing five faces (out of easily <i>hundreds</i>) by which people worship Luna, as in the Second Edition book. None of that truly helped inform what it was like to play or be a Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> If a culture worships Luna in any form, it should be something written in the description of that culture, whether in an official text or a player's character backstory or a storyteller's notes.<br /> <br /> It also kind of implicitly constricted the sorts of faces Luna would wear when appearing before your Lunar PC at Exaltation. There should be a lot more variety, there, and no one should need to explain why she doesn't appear as one of those five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:22:33-08:00","id":385047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385015#post385015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the talk of Lunars as Folk Heroes makes me think of folk tales like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chasse-galerie\" target=\"_blank\">La Chasse-Galerie</a> or whatnot, where Lunars are a bunch of Quebeckers sitting down in the woods in the dead of winter to have a beer and talk about their wives and hockey. They just happen to also be werewolves and runs-faster-than-a-speeding-train local celebrities. (With thick Joual or Acadian accents no less)<br /> <br /> Edit: oh void, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cood3ZnRJk8\" target=\"_blank\">Elvis Gratton</a> as a Folk Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know if this is what I would see Lunars being, but damn it sure is a game that I would like to play. I have been wanting to play fanciful game where you are lost or cursed to live in a world of strange folklore and faitytales. Think &quot;Over the Garden Wall&quot;, &quot;Something Wicked This Way Comes&quot;, &quot;Alice in Wonderland&quot;, &quot;1001 nights&quot;, or &quot;Hellboy: In Hell&quot; something where each session can be a strange new tale.<br /> <br /> The rumor is that the next D&amp;D campaign to be announced will be inspired by &quot;Alice in Wonderland&quot; so I am crossing my fingers for a episodic adventure set in the Feywilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:25:30-08:00","id":385049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385044#post385044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the <i>idea</i> of a Silver Pact, especially as an institution for preserving whatever's left of Creation's glorious (or occasionally deeply-horrific) past, but loathe the execution. I'd prefer to see it as a sort of loosely-affiliated support network that depends on individual initiative for starting projects but a Lunar can try to get support by selling other Lunars on the plan. Super Secret-Handshake Awesome Abduction Club for Failures can DIAF.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I'd prefer seeing it something akin to an underground Freedom-fighter Network (complete with coded long-range communications, resource-and-intel sharing, guerrilla strike-teams, deep-cover saboteurs, secret lodgings (caves, houses, etc) for missions/interrogations, etc.) instead of a bunch of lone-wolves that do their own thing in isolated towns/cultures and consider it an affront when one of their kin steps over their territory lines.<br /> <br /> Great. Now I gotta run Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy as a Lunar-Resistance-fighters game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:25:43-08:00","id":385051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385018#post385018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Glories, Luna seemed Mundane. Lack of detail doesn't automatically make one mysterious or fantastic --- it can also just result in &amp;quot;this NPC is not used at all&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;the ST defaults to the most generic, average idea they have&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;the ST copies some other lore&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Infernals are a good comparison. I <u>loved</u> them as a concept since 1E -- but we never got a write-up so I never saw an ST use them (unless it was as super-Satanic antagonists in the most cliche villain roles ever).<br /> <br /> So<br /> <br /> The theory doesn't amount to practice.<br /> <br /> And as aforementioned, Glories of Luna revitalized the splat for me (such that I was able to get concepts approved that - going just off the Lunar book - STs previously thought were too weird). Her aspects added the kind of rich yet different <b>archetypes </b>that Great Houses and Deathlords and Yozis provide everyone else with (validating more eccentric interpretations than --- what I feel --- the homogenizing Silver Pact mish-mash gave us). The word count spent on her only <i>enriched</i> Lunars, validating those who didn't want to be the 235th &amp;quot;generic glorified beastman trickster-warrior in silver ink&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to agree to it as practical or ideal (I'm not 100% sure I disagree with you on that) for it to be, nevertheless, the way the line intends to potentially operate going forward. I won't say that is the intent-- I don't know the intent-- only that this is the interpretation I would infer from the statement, rather than the other. And, then, if this interpretation IS the intent, then it'd be safe to say 2e Luna is dead and gone so far as 3e canon is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:35:49-08:00","id":385074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385015#post385015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the talk of Lunars as Folk Heroes makes me think of folk tales like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chasse-galerie\" target=\"_blank\">La Chasse-Galerie</a> or whatnot, where Lunars are a bunch of Quebeckers sitting down in the woods in the dead of winter to have a beer and talk about their wives and hockey. They just happen to also be werewolves and runs-faster-than-a-speeding-train local celebrities. (With thick Joual or Acadian accents no less)<br /> <br /> Edit: oh void, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cood3ZnRJk8\" target=\"_blank\">Elvis Gratton</a> as a Folk Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quebecois Lunars...okay, time to make that <i>Infinite Jest</i> shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:38:21-08:00","id":385077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385049#post385049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. I'd prefer seeing it something akin to an underground Freedom-fighter Network (complete with coded long-range communications, resource-and-intel sharing, guerrilla strike-teams, deep-cover saboteurs, secret lodgings (caves, houses, etc) for missions/interrogations, etc.) instead of a bunch of lone-wolves that do their own thing in isolated towns/cultures and consider it an affront when one of their kin steps over their territory lines.<br /> <br /> Great. Now I gotta run Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy as a Lunar-Resistance-fighters game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only worry if you made them too &quot;formal&quot; an organisation is that they would have the same boring bureaucratic problems as the Sidereals. Maybe instead of stuffy organisation like MI6 they could be more like the Kurds fighting to restore a homeland that has been fracture by the powers that surround them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:43:39-08:00","id":385084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385013#post385013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hrm. Isn't it relevant though? I mean, why state that less word count should be spent on describing Incarna otherwise? Do you really think such a statement would be meant to be interpreted as, &quot;we don't want to spend that kind of word count because it's already been spent? So just go look at 2e's write up for more info&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't about Luna, it's about the Exalted.<br /> <br /> They have said &quot;we want Lunars to match up with the Incarna described in the book&quot;. That is a principle that can hold true even if nothing else is ever written about that Incarna again. It is a principle that would be untrue if Lunars contained no trickster elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer seeing it something akin to an underground Freedom-fighter Network (complete with coded long-range communications, resource-and-intel sharing, guerrilla strike-teams, deep-cover saboteurs, secret lodgings (caves, houses, etc) for missions/interrogations, etc.) instead of a bunch of lone-wolves that do their own thing in isolated towns/cultures and consider it an affront when one of their kin steps over their territory lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still thinking of them in terms of Al-Qaeda, which kind of creates a happy middle ground between the two concepts; despite some of the mission statements involved, international Islamic terrorism (and its affiliates with other non-Islamic or Islamist criminal or terrorist groups) is not one big happy family, even if everybody went to training camps funded by Bin Laden money.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-29-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:51:05-08:00","id":385112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385084#post385084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't about Luna, it's about the Exalted.<br /> <br /> They have said &amp;quot;we want Lunars to match up with the Incarna described in the book&amp;quot;. That is a principle that can hold true even if nothing else is ever written about that Incarna again. It is a principle that would be untrue if Lunars contained no trickster elements.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is more question than counterpoint: did they say they wanted Exalted to match up with the presentation of Incarnae in Glories? If so, though I've not heard it, then sure, I buy your argument. <br /> <br /> If they want, instead, Exalted to match what little they will say about the Incarnae in the Ex3 core, rather...well, we don't know what that is or will be yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:52:39-08:00","id":385115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385077#post385077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only worry if you made them too &quot;formal&quot; an organisation is that they would have the same boring bureaucratic problems as the Sidereals. Maybe instead of stuffy organisation like MI6 they could be more like the Kurds fighting to restore a homeland that has been fracture by the powers that surround them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely, I was thinking Kurds.<br /> TTSS would be in a Modern game (I watched it recently for a Demon game that fell through and have been itching to run something like it ever since), I wouldn't have Bestial/Folkloric stylistically-Barbarian demigods be stained by a tightly-knit bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385074#post385074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quebecois Lunars...okay, time to make that <i>Infinite Jest</i> shard.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea how happy that would make me and my circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T09:01:58-08:00","id":385122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385112#post385112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this is more question than counterpoint: did they say they wanted Exalted to match up with the presentation of Incarnae in Glories? If so, though I've not heard it, then sure, I buy your argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that Luna was John's favourite thing that he wrote for Glories. Holden used to say things along the lines of looking forward to turning the Lunars into Exalted worthy of the god written in that book, and on the occasion where John broke down how all of the Exalted were different such that there was no generic competence, his description of Lunars amounted to a list of traits that was punctuated with &quot;just like Luna&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T09:36:05-08:00","id":385178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385074#post385074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quebecois Lunars...okay, time to make that <i>Infinite Jest</i> shard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have been seriously considering a Heaven's Canoe Style, since that's the sort of thing you really <i>do </i>need to carry around all the time when you're out adventuring. It remains to be seen whether the stupidity or awesomeness of the idea will win, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T13:36:34-08:00","id":385512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=384423#post384423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human history is full of trickters.<br /> <br /> If you can only be a trickster with GODLIKE AMAZING POWER, then you're probably not clever enough to be a trickster.<br /> <br /> Same goes for all other categories. Believe it or not, there have been epic orators, warriors, sages, etc without magic (such that in some cases, magic was later ascribed).<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> Someone who enjoys playing manipulative bastards</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank god you're here to clear that up for me. Who knows how long, if ever, it would take me to reach such an enlightened conclusion. Not like I'm talking about powers specific to the splat in question. <br /> <br /> Noooo, no-no-no, I want to make sure Lunars are capable of using trickery at the basic human level without charms. As if for some reason the splat as a whole would only be capable of honesty and forthright dealings unless specifically enumerated in a charm text.<br /> <br /> I mean, a reader more capable of abstract thought may imagine I was posting about the Lunars/those characters ability to cause others to doubt their perceptions and basic understanding of the world. That illusion would cover hallucination, mirage, obsession and dream; the uncanny state that may be impossible to describe but hauntingly familiar. The ability for a Lunar to know what you desire when you do not. Mystery and instinct and the will-o-wisp just at the threshold between knowing and doubt.<br /> <br /> Nooo, you saw through into all that subtext to what really needed to be said, that there's no reason a lunar can't be clever or manipulative just because he or she doesn't have charms for it.<br /> <br /> Awesome. Great news. I suppose everything is just absolutely fine then. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 01-29-2015, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T13:59:56-08:00","id":385527,"title":"","content":"You're welcome bro. #yoloswag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T15:03:44-08:00","id":385594,"title":"","content":"Lunars are still going to have a pile of Manipulation charms, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:21:05-08:00","id":385688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385512#post385512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, thank god you're here to clear that up for me. Who knows how long, if ever, it would take me to reach such an enlightened conclusion. Not like I'm talking about powers specific to the splat in question.<br /> <br /> Noooo, no-no-no, I want to make sure Lunars are capable of using trickery at the basic human level without charms. As if for some reason the splat as a whole would only be capable of honesty and forthright dealings unless specifically enumerated in a charm text.<br /> <br /> I mean, a reader more capable of abstract thought may imagine I was posting about the Lunars/those characters ability to cause others to doubt their perceptions and basic understanding of the world. That illusion would cover hallucination, mirage, obsession and dream; the uncanny state that may be impossible to describe but hauntingly familiar. The ability for a Lunar to know what you desire when you do not. Mystery and instinct and the will-o-wisp just at the threshold between knowing and doubt.<br /> <br /> Nooo, you saw through into all that subtext to what really needed to be said, that there's no reason a lunar can't be clever or manipulative just because he or she doesn't have charms for it.<br /> <br /> Awesome. Great news. I suppose everything is just absolutely fine then. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Waiter, I'd like some pepper with this salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:26:00-08:00","id":385690,"title":"","content":"Mythology is my jam, and I really enjoyed writing Glories, and I am floored that people love my origin for Luna there so much. <br /> <br /> You will find bits of her bio in Glories referenced in EX3, and soon. But there are some parts that are deliberately, mysteriously going to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:45:34-08:00","id":385695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385690#post385690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will find bits of her bio in Glories referenced in EX3, and soon. But there are some parts that are deliberately, mysteriously going to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Why am I not surprised that Luna is able to change her backstory to fit a new edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:05:56-08:00","id":385707,"title":"","content":"I look forward to see how Luna changes to fit the new edition as much as I look forward to seeing lunars finally being given their due in setting instead of most of them just standing around twiddling their thumbs and maybe playing god to a tribe of barbarians in the ass end of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:07:05-08:00","id":385708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385695#post385695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Why am I not surprised that Luna is able to change her backstory to fit a new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point, does being the ultimate mutable god make her easier or harder to write for? I guess it depends on if the writer prefers working from a specific foundation, or having the possibility to go in whatever direction catches their interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:41:37-08:00","id":385728,"title":"","content":"I liked Glories Luna as an allegory for how there are many competing, related but incompatible visions of Lunars and they battle endlessly in the hopes of triumphing and becoming the True Lunars. I assume that wasn't the intention at all, but it's the most fun reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:54:47-08:00","id":385738,"title":"","content":"As a note, folks are tossing about the 300 Lunars thing somewhat. Remember that something stated a bit ago is that for Celestials at least they're going to less fixed numbers on their total population (more &quot;around n number of Exalts&quot; sort of stuff). And in this it was noted that there is something like around 400 Lunars, while still around (not exaclty) 300ish Solars and their derivatives.<br /> <br /> This means there's now kind of a specific asymmetry with the whole Lunar/Solar relationship and a hundred more Lunars to do the world dominating and insurgency thing. Not that it changes the whole discussion going on now, but something I thought worth pointing out.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T20:02:56-08:00","id":385739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385738#post385738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, folks are tossing about the 300 Lunars thing somewhat. Remember that something stated a bit ago is that for Celestials at least they're going to less fixed numbers on their total population (more &quot;around n number of Exalts&quot; sort of stuff). And in this it was noted that there is something like around 400 Lunars, while still around (not exaclty) 300ish Solars and their derivatives.<br /> <br /> This means there's now kind of a specific asymmetry with the whole Lunar/Solar relationship and a hundred more Lunars to do the world dominating and insurgency thing. Not that it changes the whole discussion going on now, but something I thought worth pointing out.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they didn't clarify whether 300 solars meant they were changing the setting so there are 300 solars running around present day plus the ones that got turned into another exalt type or if it was still going to be the same as 2E and be 'used to be 300 solars but now a lot of those are something else'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T20:12:52-08:00","id":385744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385739#post385739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, they didn't clarify whether 300 solars meant they were changing the setting so there are 300 solars running around present day plus the ones that got turned into another exalt type or if it was still going to be the same as 2E and be 'used to be 300 solars but now a lot of those are something else'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most striclty it was about 150ish Solars and 100ish Abyssals. But you are right in that this doesn't mean them and the original hinted-at 50 (if they're sitll there) Infernals will be the same thing originally. But that at the same time weakens the idea of Solar-Lunar parity as a mandatory thing further.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T20:17:33-08:00","id":385765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385708#post385708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good point, does being the ultimate mutable god make her easier or harder to write for? I guess it depends on if the writer prefers working from a specific foundation, or having the possibility to go in whatever direction catches their interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess there's some degree of foundation in play for most gods that have any Exalted. At least in cases where the concept for that Exalted type is conceived first. The nature of those Exalts is somewhat set, what with the writers having some idea of the themes, powers, play styles, etc. they're likely to have. This sets some constraints on how the god can be written, as the god's nature needs to be such that it would give rise to Chosen with those capabilities.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine sometimes things can go in reverse, too, where especially compelling concepts or depictions of gods are the core foundations for the Exalted they'd create. ... On second thought, this probably goes both ways much of the time, with needs/inspirations for the splat feeding/demanding changes to the writing of the patron, which in turn impacts the writing of the splat again, and on and on for a while. As the Exalted are generally player options and more likely than the god to appear/impact an actual game, though, I imagine the way the Exalts are conceived and written generally takes precedence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, I definitely want these Exalts to have/be X, Y, and Z. So maybe their god could have/be... Yeah, there's a good start. Let's see where it goes. ... Ooh, ooh! I just thought of a really cool power for which she's known! I'm going to make sure her Chosen get that, or at least reflect it in some way. Hrrm... Yeah! That's the way. Though in hindsight, it clashes something fierce with Y and makes Z a little redundant, so I guess Y doesn't really fit for these Exalts anymore. I guess I can try to weave Z into the newcomer, or... Wait, if I emphasize that part of it in this way and put it into a splat-specific sub-system, then... Ohhh, that makes me happy. And it works great in the god's writeup to tone down Y's inspiration and add these cool new details. I think we're really getting somewhere!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T20:47:28-08:00","id":385789,"title":"","content":"One thing I hope the writers keep in mind is that there really shouldn't be any (or many) First Age Lunars running around. In order to be a First Age surviver you have to survive the Usurpation, the Shogunate version of the Wyld Hunt, the Great Contagion, the Fair Folk invasion, and the Wyld Hunt v 2.0 outside of dying to things like old age and Sidreals/accidents. I do hope that they limit themselves to only about 1 or 2 First Age survivors and focus most of the NPC word count on Lunar Elders from the Shogunate and the early Realm. These eras didn't get enough coverage in 2nd ed anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T20:57:36-08:00","id":385810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385789#post385789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I hope the writers keep in mind is that there really shouldn't be any (or many) First Age Lunars running around. In order to be a First Age surviver you have to survive the Usurpation, the Shogunate version of the Wyld Hunt, the Great Contagion, the Fair Folk invasion, and the Wyld Hunt v 2.0 outside of dying to things like old age and Sidreals/accidents. I do hope that they limit themselves to only about 1 or 2 First Age survivors and focus most of the NPC word count on Lunar Elders from the Shogunate and the early Realm. These eras didn't get enough coverage in 2nd ed anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the Lunars have still fled to the Wyld at some point even if it isn't their base of operations now? If there were still elder Lunars emerging from the Wylds every once in a while I could see it explained through timey-whimy shenanigans, imagine if what felt like a year to the Lunar was actually centuries to the rest of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:24:42-08:00","id":385822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385789#post385789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I hope the writers keep in mind is that there really shouldn't be any (or many) First Age Lunars running around. In order to be a First Age surviver you have to survive the Usurpation, the Shogunate version of the Wyld Hunt, the Great Contagion, the Fair Folk invasion, and the Wyld Hunt v 2.0 outside of dying to things like old age and Sidreals/accidents. I do hope that they limit themselves to only about 1 or 2 First Age survivors and focus most of the NPC word count on Lunar Elders from the Shogunate and the early Realm. These eras didn't get enough coverage in 2nd ed anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would require removing or rewriting a lot of currently existing lunar elders, but we definitely need new Lunar NPCs who are from those eras since every lunar in 2nd ED I can think of off the top of my head is either a first age survivor or a noob who only exalted recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:27:25-08:00","id":385824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385810#post385810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will the Lunars have still fled to the Wyld at some point even if it isn't their base of operations now? If there were still elder Lunars emerging from the Wylds every once in a while I could see it explained through timey-whimy shenanigans, imagine if what felt like a year to the Lunar was actually centuries to the rest of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to do that at least make the Lunar do something like &quot;Hey guys, there are 10 million Raksha coming right this way!!!! Wait, why isn't everything dying like it was a couple days ago?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:40:59-08:00","id":385828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385824#post385824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to do that at least make the Lunar do something like &quot;Hey guys, there are 10 million Raksha coming right this way!!!! Wait, why isn't everything dying like it was a couple days ago?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a &quot;canon&quot; thing, another crusade hurtling towards creation? If it is I could see that plot-line disappearing in EX3, I feel like they are going to some effort to get rid of the &quot;press this button to destroy Creation&quot; plots like the crazy Deathlord super-weapons, and the Yozi reclamation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:45:38-08:00","id":385832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385828#post385828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a &quot;canon&quot; thing, another crusade hurtling towards creation? If it is I could see that plot-line disappearing in EX3, I feel like they are going to some effort to get rid of the &quot;press this button to destroy Creation&quot; plots like the crazy Deathlord super-weapons, and the Yozi reclamation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was more of a &quot;the Balorian Crusade is on the way and I think the Great Contagion is still ongoing&quot; thing. In my demented head I was thinking around the lines of a person out of time warning me that the British were coming and I needed to get my musket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T22:00:54-08:00","id":385841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385832#post385832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it was more of a &quot;the Balorian Crusade is on the way and I think the Great Contagion is still ongoing&quot; thing. In my demented head I was thinking around the lines of a person out of time warning me that the British were coming and I needed to get my musket.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gotcha, hell for a elder Lunar it would be the other way around. Lunar elder walks out of the Wylds and into a tiny village &quot;what is that smell...it's the people...uggh whats wrong with him...does he have consumption...direct me to the the nearest skyship port immediately...blank stares because the don't speak Old Realm...&quot;. An elder Lunar travelling forward in time is actually travelling back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T22:12:14-08:00","id":385850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385841#post385841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh gotcha, hell for a elder Lunar it would be the other way around. Lunar elder walks out of the Wylds and into a tiny village &quot;what is that smell...it's the people...uggh whats wrong with him...does he have consumption...direct me to the the nearest skyship port immediately...blank stares because the don't speak Old Realm...&quot;. An elder Lunar travelling forward in time is actually travelling back in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I suggest that we avoid time travel to keep fragile Lunar brains from shattering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Besides the brain pudding, I don't think that I've read any time travel story that really took narrative advantage of it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T22:58:01-08:00","id":385889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385850#post385850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. I suggest that we avoid time travel to keep fragile Lunar brains from shattering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Besides the brain pudding, I don't think that I've read any time travel story that really took narrative advantage of it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant travel through time in Exalted, every moment only ever happens once...though there was that time where...well time, started running out of order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:04:18-08:00","id":385907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385822#post385822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would require removing or rewriting a lot of currently existing lunar elders...</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve of this message <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:05:58-08:00","id":385908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385889#post385889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cant travel through time in Exalted, every moment only ever happens once...though there was that time where...well time, started running out of order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase then. Let's avoid the &quot;timey-whimy shenanigans&quot;. It gives most people a headache anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:14:18-08:00","id":385914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385907#post385907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I approve of this message <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could always get rid of Leviathan, lazy fish bastard just floats around playing sims and writing emo poetry in his head involving terrible things happening to dragon blooded. At least Raksi is trying to break setting rules and learn solar circle sorcery while she is lazing around ignoring the rest of the world, he literally just floats around moping like a sad sack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:33:35-08:00","id":385965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385914#post385914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We could always get rid of Leviathan, lazy fish bastard just floats around playing sims and writing emo poetry in his head involving terrible things happening to dragon blooded. At least Raksi is trying to break setting rules and learn solar circle sorcery while she is lazing around ignoring the rest of the world, he literally just floats around moping like a sad sack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathan could be SO freaking cool if he had some motivations, but he was always written with so much mystery and hemming and hawing on the truth of him that he basically became a folk tale. I remember somebody suggesting that he could be stuck in the form of a giant living factory cathedral/genesis complex, but I can't remember if that was canon or just a fan idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:43:08-08:00","id":385992,"title":"","content":"It definitely wasn't from a canon work, he is just a lunar who has voluntarily been in his abnormally huge whale form for centuries and swims around Luthe moping. He doesn't even directly rule the city, he lets a younger lunar do it and only rarely passes instructions along to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:49:43-08:00","id":385996,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Luthe, I can't wait to see what they do with it this time around. It had so many awesome things mixed in with the stupid, like the awesome blurb about it being made from the ocean itself by a group of solars and dragon blooded working in tandem which was preceded by the book murdering any sense of wonder by saying it was named 'Mobile Platform 3' when it was created.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what the hell? Primordial war exalts couldn't take five seconds to name their amazing moving island city and just named it based on order of creation compared to other giant moving city wonders in the other directions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T23:58:28-08:00","id":385999,"title":"","content":"Leviathan should be an ancient chimera in EX3. A huge whale/octopus thing that lurks in Sunken Luthe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T00:00:00-08:00","id":386001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385996#post385996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Luthe, I can't wait to see what they do with it this time around. It had so many awesome things mixed in with the stupid, like the awesome blurb about it being made from the ocean itself by a group of solars and dragon blooded working in tandem which was preceded by the book murdering any sense of wonder by saying it was named 'Mobile Platform 3' when it was created.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what the hell? Primordial war exalts couldn't take five seconds to name their amazing moving island city and just named it based on order of creation compared to other giant moving city wonders in the other directions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya that doesn't have much of a ring to it...but maybe they were writing under the assumption that to the first age Solars it really was just Mobile Platform 3, a logistical necessity, not a military flagship or glorious flying palace deserving of a more epic name. Really though even oil platforms get cool names, Deepwater Horizon, Deepsea Stavanger, Thunderhorse, Mad Dog, all names of real installations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T00:17:27-08:00","id":386014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385999#post385999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan should be an ancient chimera in EX3. A huge whale/octopus thing that lurks in Sunken Luthe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Kireeki? No, I think that if he ends up as a chimera, it should combine something different than what she has. Hopefully, he can at least regain some of the grandeur of being a force of nature to make up for everything in the last edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:12:18-08:00","id":386371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/382269-3e-lunars-facts-and-speculation?p=385728#post385728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Glories Luna as an allegory for how there are many competing, related but incompatible visions of Lunars and they battle endlessly in the hopes of triumphing and becoming the True Lunars. <b>I assume that wasn't the intention at all</b>, but it's the most fun reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you assume that? It seems like a reasonable influence to me.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone who proposed concept after concept, across two Editions and edging into a third, for re-envisioning the Lunar Exalted to make them not suck.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}